window.LLaDARSearchIndex = {"version":1,"documents":[{"url":"examples/support-demo-agent.html","lang":"en","title":"Support demo Agent","sections":[{"heading":"What this example represents","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"The Agent answers questions about a simple support plan: business-day email support, a one-business-day reply target, and an on-call process for urgent incidents. It uses only the Python standard library. It is an Agent to test, not a replacement for LLaDAR's configured model provider."},{"heading":"Public contract","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"The user-facing route is HTTP POST /api/chat . Send {\"input\":{\"text\":\"What is the standard reply target?\"}} ; the response is {\"data\":{\"answer\":\"...\"}} . GET /health shows whether the service is ready."},{"heading":"Let LLaDAR manage the project","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"lladar run-agent dataset.jsonl --project examples/support-demo-agent --no-interactive --output responses.jsonl LLaDAR inspects the project, checks the selected route, then uses it for the dataset."},{"heading":"Use it as an existing test service","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"Start the service in one terminal: python examples/support-demo-agent/server.py --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 Then give LLaDAR that exact URL: lladar run-agent dataset.jsonl --project examples/support-demo-agent --service-url http://127.0.0.1:8000 --no-interactive --output responses.jsonl LLaDAR will not start or stop a service supplied through --service-url ."},{"heading":"How the example is verified","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"tests/test_support_demo_agent.py checks policy answers, GET /health , and the public POST /api/chat route without provider credentials. A full LLaDAR run additionally needs configured provider credentials."}]},{"url":"getting-started.html","lang":"en","title":"Run one complete evaluation","sections":[{"heading":"Before you begin","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"Python 3.11 or 3.12. Credentials for the LLaDAR model provider, in .env or the process environment. A clone of this repository for the included demo Agent. The demo Agent itself needs only Python. Dataset generation, evaluation, and reporting use your configured provider."},{"heading":"Optional: plan the test first","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"If you know what you want to investigate but are unsure which LLaDAR stages or inputs are needed, use the interactive planner: lladar plan \"Check whether my support Agent follows the refund documents\" --debug The planner asks only for missing information, then produces a validated plan and the commands for the requested workflow. It does not call the target Agent and does not run dataset generation, testing, evaluation, or reporting. By default, the plan is saved under runs/plan-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS/ . Inspect plan.md and plan.json before running the suggested commands. A ready plan passed static checks; it does not prove that the target is reachable or that a test will succeed. See the plan command reference for options and status details."},{"heading":"1. Install LLaDAR and obtain the demo","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"git clone https://github.com/stoday/LLaDAR.git cd LLaDAR python -m pip install -e ."},{"heading":"2. Create questions from the support policy","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"lladar create test-dataset --knowledge examples/support-demo-agent/knowledge.md --output demo-dataset.jsonl This creates questions and expected answers based on the policy."},{"heading":"3. Run the demo Agent","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"lladar run-agent demo-dataset.jsonl --project examples/support-demo-agent --no-interactive --output demo-responses.jsonl LLaDAR finds the demo Agent's public entry point, checks that it can use it, and records the responses."},{"heading":"4. Evaluate answers and create a report","anchor":"doc-search-section-6","text":"lladar eval demo-responses.jsonl --output demo-evaluation.json lladar report demo-evaluation.json --output demo-report.md"},{"heading":"What success looks like","anchor":"doc-search-section-7","text":"File What it shows demo-dataset.jsonl The questions and expected answers. demo-responses.jsonl The Agent's answer for each question. demo-responses.jsonl.run.json How LLaDAR reached the Agent and whether the replay worked. demo-evaluation.json and demo-report.md Per-question judgments and a readable summary. Important: a successful replay proves that the Agent entry point was exercised. Use the saved evaluation and report to assess answer quality."},{"heading":"Next path: multi-turn situations","anchor":"doc-search-section-8","text":"To observe behavior across a conversation without a required knowledge file, follow the copyable situation example . It creates a configuration, calibrates a session adapter, saves transcripts, and evaluates the completed turns."}]},{"url":"guides/create-dataset.html","lang":"en","title":"Create a test dataset","sections":[{"heading":"What this step does","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"lladar create test-dataset reads knowledge files or directories and writes records with a question, expected answer, and an empty place for the Agent's later response."},{"heading":"Discover a GitHub dataset","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"lladar create test-dataset --from-github https://github.com/hsinmosyi/TWBias --count 20 --output dataset.jsonl Choose --knowledge or --from-github . The Agent finds actual public text datasets and records answer origins. Every output question is covered by dataset.generation-report.md , with source excerpts, fixed-version links, transformations, model checks and limits. Saved originals are in dataset.sources.json . Review generated criteria before running the target Agent."},{"heading":"Basic command","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"lladar create test-dataset --knowledge KNOWLEDGE_PATH --output dataset.jsonl Repeat --knowledge to combine inputs. An output ending in .jsonl names the exact file; an output directory receives a new timestamped dataset."},{"heading":"Choose a generation method","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"The Agent follows the selected Skill: it can generate questions directly from source passages or use an evidence graph for concept probes. Graphs are optional. Final candidates are validated before publishing; a .graph.json sidecar is written only when a valid graph is used."},{"heading":"Use a custom local Skill","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"Pass one --skill DIRECTORY to use your own generation method. The directory must contain SKILL.md . For example, a support team can require questions about returns, delivery, and refunds. lladar create test-dataset --knowledge policy/ --skill skills/support-qa --output dataset.jsonl"},{"heading":"Watch token usage","anchor":"doc-search-section-6","text":"From v0.17.0, create test-dataset accumulates the input and output tokens reported by the model provider. Verbose output is enabled by default: a [TOKENS] line updates the cumulative counts after each model response, including tool rounds and retries. It does not update token by token while a response is pending. lladar create test-dataset --knowledge policy/ --output dataset.jsonl --verbose --log logs/create.log For example, an update may look like this; the numbers below are illustrative: [TOKENS] stage=generation cumulative input=4000 output=600 total=4600; unreported calls=0 LLaDAR reads usage returned with the existing model response through Akasha/LangChain. Collecting these counts does not send the prompt again or make an extra token-count API call. Inventory, reconciliation, generation, audit, coverage review and repair calls contribute to the total when those stages run. --no-verbose hides these updates while still saving usage. --resume retains the work-session totals; the operation report also shows the usage added by the current invocation. Missing provider usage is unknown, not zero, and older runs cannot be reconstructed from their text. See token fields and accounting limits ."},{"heading":"Inspect the result","anchor":"doc-search-section-7","text":"Read the dataset before testing an Agent. Its .generation.json sidecar records the sources, selected Skill, settings, any skipped input, and a token_usage summary with totals and per-stage counts. Usage is also saved in the work-session checkpoint and dataset.jsonl.operation.md . You can include the saved usage in a coverage report ."},{"heading":"Need to test a conversation?","anchor":"doc-search-section-8","text":"If your goal is to observe behavior over multiple turns, use create situation . A knowledge file is optional there."}]},{"url":"guides/evaluate.html","lang":"en","title":"Evaluate completed answers","sections":[{"heading":"Basic command","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"lladar eval responses.jsonl --output evaluation.json The default method compares the expected answer from your knowledge documents with the Agent's actual response and saves a judgment for each completed trial. It is not a complete hallucination check."},{"heading":"Why save individual judgments?","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"Each judgment explains one result. Python then counts those saved results to calculate totals and rates. That keeps the summary consistent when you recreate a report."},{"heading":"Use a custom evaluation Skill","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"Your SKILL.md can say what matters for your domain. A support policy Skill, for example, can check refund deadlines and required caveats. To judge unsupported promises reliably, the method also needs suitable source evidence; a custom Skill does not make missing evidence appear. lladar eval responses.jsonl --skill skills/policy-verdict --output evaluation.json"},{"heading":"Inspect the result","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"evaluation.json contains the plan, per-question judgments, saved Skill information, and the calculated summary. An execution error shows that the run failed for that question; it does not show that the Agent gave a wrong answer."},{"heading":"Judge a multi-turn conversation","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"For situation transcripts, run lladar eval transcripts.jsonl --situation-config situation.json --output evaluation.json . The saved run must match the config hash. Judgments cite turn IDs; execution errors and indeterminate trials are excluded from the observed rate. The config already fixes the method, so --skill is rejected. Read situation results."}]},{"url":"guides/report.html","lang":"en","title":"Create an evaluation report","sections":[{"heading":"Basic command","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"lladar report evaluation.json --output report.md The positional EVALUATION points to the previous evaluation JSON. --output names the Markdown report to create."},{"heading":"What the report includes","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"What was tested and the overall result. Per-question judgments and their reasons. How the totals were calculated from the saved results. The scope and limits of this run."},{"heading":"Review dataset coverage and token usage","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"lladar report dataset.jsonl.generation.json --output dataset-coverage.md Use the generation sidecar to review independently inventoried facts and question coverage. From v0.17.0, when the sidecar contains token_usage , this report also includes the saved input/output totals, per-stage usage and accounting limits. Rendering this saved coverage report with the default method does not make another model call. The original dataset command also writes dataset.jsonl.operation.md , with the work-session token total and usage added by that invocation. Resume keeps the cumulative total; a missing usage record is unknown, not zero. Older sidecars without token records cannot provide retrospective totals. These figures describe dataset generation; see the fields and limits before comparing them with a provider bill."},{"heading":"Use it to improve the Agent","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"Do not treat the report as only a score. Group failed questions: is the source material unclear, did the Agent ignore a rule, or did the test miss an important real-world situation? Improve the relevant part, then run the same workflow again."},{"heading":"Use a custom report Skill","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"A SKILL.md can request your team's sections, tone, or review fields. The individual results and calculated totals remain available so readers can trace a conclusion back to the evidence. lladar report evaluation.json --skill skills/compliance-summary --output report.md"},{"heading":"Situation reports","anchor":"doc-search-section-6","text":"lladar report evaluation.json --output report.md renders situation counts and cited turn evidence without another model call by default. An optional --skill DIRECTORY adds narrative but does not change the saved judgments or totals. See the situation artifacts."}]},{"url":"guides/run-agent.html","lang":"en","title":"Run an existing Agent","sections":[{"heading":"Choose a project, service URL, or page URL","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"All three paths collect Agent answers into actual_response ; they differ in how LLaDAR learns to send a question. What you have Options How it works Project source and sufficient runtime setup --project PATH Inspect the public workflow; start a service in the isolated project copy when needed. Project source and an already running test service --project PATH --service-url URL Learn the API contract from the project; call the service at the supplied base address without starting or stopping it. A normal question webpage, without project source --page-url URL Sign in and calibrate in the browser, record the request for replay, and extract answers with the model. --project tells LLaDAR where to learn how to call the Agent ; --service-url tells it which already running service to call . The latter is optional, not a startup command or a substitute for an API contract. --page-url cannot be combined with --project or --service-url . If neither target option is supplied, project mode uses the current directory ( . ). The option is named --service-url , not --service-api ."},{"heading":"What project mode automates","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"Copy and inspect the target project without changing its source. Find a likely public way to send a question to the Agent. Try that route first, then use it for all scheduled questions. Save each answer and the execution record. Finding an internal function is not enough. LLaDAR first checks that the selected route can actually be replayed."},{"heading":"Path A: let LLaDAR handle a local project","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"lladar run-agent dataset.jsonl --project PATH_TO_AGENT --output responses.jsonl A project alone can be enough. LLaDAR inspects the README, startup scripts and public interface definitions. When the required runtime, dependencies and configuration are available, it can start the original service in an isolated project copy, wait for readiness, test it, and stop only the service it started. You do not need to provide --service-url in this case. If startup, authentication, or request/response details are missing, LLaDAR pauses for clarification rather than inventing them. An interactive run can ask you to choose among plausible public interfaces."},{"heading":"Path B: use an existing test service","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"lladar run-agent dataset.jsonl --project PATH_TO_AGENT --service-url http://127.0.0.1:8000 --output responses.jsonl Use --service-url when you already run a controlled test service. LLaDAR uses that exact base address and the API routes discovered in the project; it does not start or stop the existing service. The project is still required to understand the HTTP method, route, payload, authentication requirements, and response format. For example, if the project defines POST /ask with a JSON question body, http://127.0.0.1:8000 supplies the base address; it does not describe /ask or the body schema. A bare API URL is not enough to discover an arbitrary contract. Supply required credentials through the configured environment, not the URL; the URL must use HTTP(S) and must not contain credentials, a query, or a fragment."},{"heading":"Path C: provide a question page and sign in","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"Use this when you know the normal question page but not its API method, payload, or Cookie. Project source is not required. Request recording remains necessary to learn how to send questions; the model extracts answers from the responses, not the request contract. First run python -m playwright install chromium , then: lladar run-agent dataset.jsonl --page-url https://example.test/chat --output responses.jsonl --page-url always uses the guided sign-in, calibration, consent and MATCH workflow. Omit --interactive and --no-interactive ; these project-only options are rejected in browser mode. Run directly in a terminal with stdin and stderr attached. Piped input or redirected stderr stops the CLI before opening the browser, even with both approval flags. Browser answers are extracted directly by a tool-free model, default gemini:gemini-3.8-flash . There is no generated Python, built-in answer-rule mode, Monty, or parser cache. Configure GEMINI_API_KEY or GOOGLE_API_KEY in the environment or --env-file ; credentials are initialized only after calibration and approval. Sign in yourself in the visible LLaDAR browser and submit the exact calibration question. Wait for completion, then press Enter. Review website requests, model destination and budgets together. One YES approves both website requests and sending real response content, including internal answers, to https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com . Check your organization's data policy first. Compare the newly extracted verification answer against its complete recording in the terminal (stderr); type MATCH only when faithful and complete. Then dataset execution begins. No HTML review tab opens. Cyan source headings, magenta extracted-answer headings and yellow notices identify sections, not correctness. NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb selects plain text. Full content is quoted, not truncated; backslashes and control/format characters are escaped for display without changing saved answers. Terminal scrollback or recording may retain private content. Redirected review output is refused. Chromium is still required for sign-in/capture; there is no new browser-free mode or per-dataset-answer MATCH. --confirm-browser-run and --allow-response-model-transfer approve only their own scopes for this run. Neither bypasses independent review or the CLI terminal requirement. A valid model result or one successful review does not guarantee later extraction fidelity or answer correctness; evaluate separately. Browser startup, initial navigation and reload each allow 5 minutes (300 seconds), independently of --timeout . Website answers still default to 60 minutes ( --timeout 3600 ); automatic replay is also capped by the remaining shared deadline. N scheduled trials, including repeats, permit at most N+2 model calls: calibration, verification, then one per trial. Each call has at most 8,192 output tokens; all calls and intervening verification share 60 minutes after approval. No automatic retries, redirects, answer caching or hidden website replay. Provider usage is recorded when available, otherwise unknown; charges may apply. Native WebSocket supports sequential text/JSON question frames when the server normally closes each answer connection (code 1000). Cookies and subprotocols remain in the controlled browser. Calibration can select DOM fallback from the same completed interaction for persistent or binary protocols. Supported DOM layouts are native Streamlit chat (validated with 1.65.0) and accessible form chats with unique inputs, named buttons/logs, user/assistant message roles and busy-to-idle completion, including named same-origin iframes. Verification and dataset trials keep the selected route; failures stop later submissions. Other layouts need adaptation. Text, JSON/+json, NDJSON, GraphQL-over-HTTP JSON and SSE are model inputs. Capture is limited to 1 MiB of decoded bytes; model input is separately limited to 120 KiB of UTF-8 JSON including framing, reserving fixed-prompt space under a local 128 KiB byte budget. This is not a tokenizer guarantee. No truncation, summarization or automatic chunking. The host does not select answer fields or terminal events. Open automatic streams time out rather than producing partial answers. Credentials, request headers/body, profile data and expected answers are excluded from model input. Known echoed credentials or credential-like response fields block transfer; detection cannot guarantee that all private content is found. No raw streams, prompts, provider diagnostics or thoughts are written to normal artifacts. Final text remains actual_response in responses/trials; safe run metadata records model/prompt version, counts, usage and status. Reuse the dedicated local .lladar/browser-profiles session, or choose --fresh-browser-profile for a temporary signed-out profile; ordinary Chrome/Edge profiles are never imported. On 401/403 or extraction failure, later requests stop and completed answers remain. Sign in and approve a new run; no authentication retry is sent. Removed parser flags are rejected, and old private caches are left unused and untouched. --page-url cannot be combined with --project or --service-url . Use the target selection table if you also have project source."},{"heading":"Project mode: interactive and unattended runs","anchor":"doc-search-section-6","text":"If more than one public route seems plausible, an interactive terminal can ask you to choose. Use --no-interactive only when the intended route is clear. These interaction options apply only to project mode; website testing always follows its guided terminal workflow."},{"heading":"Multi-turn situation mode","anchor":"doc-search-section-7","text":"Use run-agent --situation-config situation.json --project PATH --num-scenarios N to generate starting scenarios and run conversations. The supplied or generated session adapter must pass two-turn and fresh-session calibration before scored tests. This mode saves transcripts and different sidecars; DATASET and --skill cannot be combined with the situation config. Read the full situation guide."},{"heading":"What to inspect afterwards","anchor":"doc-search-section-8","text":"File What it shows responses.jsonl Completed questions and actual responses. responses.jsonl.trials.jsonl The records and repeats that were scheduled. responses.jsonl.run.json Discovery, selected route, replay, and run status. If browser calibration, confirmation, or verification stops before dataset execution, LLaDAR writes only a redacted .run.json blocker record; it does not create responses or trials files. Important: verified means replay succeeded. It is not a judgment about answer quality."}]},{"url":"guides/situations.html","lang":"en","title":"Test behavior across a conversation","sections":[{"heading":"Choose the test","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"Goal Create Run output Check answers against a knowledge-based expected answer create test-dataset --knowledge Single-question, three-field responses JSONL Observe behavior in an adaptive conversation create situation ; knowledge optional Conversation transcripts JSONL Both paths use run-agent , eval , and report . A situation configuration stores variation axes, the conversation method, stopping limit, and a fixed evaluation rubric. It does not require a prewritten answer."},{"heading":"Run the included example","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"From the repository root, use Python 3.11 or 3.12, uv , and working Gemini credentials in .env or the environment. The target here is the small local application in example_project/situation_demo ; Gemini authors the situation, generates follow-ups, and judges transcripts. uv run lladar create situation --instructions \"Observe whether the assistant remains consistent about needing an order number across a follow-up conversation and avoids inventing order status\" --stop-criteria \"Continue until at least two user messages have been sent and the assistant has replied to the follow-up, or stop at the maximum turn limit\" --max-turns 3 --output .tmp/situation-site-demo/situation.json --model gemini:gemini-3.8-flash uv run lladar run-agent --situation-config .tmp/situation-site-demo/situation.json --project example_project/situation_demo --num-scenarios 2 --output .tmp/situation-site-demo/transcripts.jsonl --model gemini:gemini-3.8-flash uv run lladar eval .tmp/situation-site-demo/transcripts.jsonl --situation-config .tmp/situation-site-demo/situation.json --output .tmp/situation-site-demo/evaluation.json --model gemini:gemini-3.8-flash uv run lladar report .tmp/situation-site-demo/evaluation.json --output .tmp/situation-site-demo/report.md Use new output paths for another run, or pass --force when you intend to replace existing files. Add repeatable --knowledge PATH for existing .md or .txt files when the behavior depends on reference material."},{"heading":"What the configuration fixes","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"situation.json stores the observation, stopping text and maximum turns, knowledge file hashes, fixed constraints, declared variation axes and values, three versioned method instructions, and an evaluation rubric. A custom --skill DIRECTORY applies only while create situation writes this configuration. With --situation-config , run-agent keeps the fixed execution methods and rejects its scheduling Skill. Eval uses the fixed rubric by default; mutually exclusive --criteria TEXT or --skill DIRECTORY replaces evaluation for the saved dialogue without changing the original config. Results record the effective evaluation settings. Scenarios record their selected variation and first user message. The next user message is generated after reading the target's actual response. The target receives user messages, not the hidden observation or rubric."},{"heading":"Calibrate a multi-turn adapter before scored tests","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"The project can supply lladar_session.py . Otherwise LLaDAR writes a candidate adapter in a project copy. Both project modes share coding-agent discovery, source/search/graph tools, public-interface selection and verified repair. With max_turns=1 , calibration checks a single real answer without requiring memory. For multi-turn settings it tests two messages in one session: the second must recall a random token from the first. A new session must have a distinct ID and must not recall that token. Requests and responses must correlate by session ID and turn ID. A failed calibration stops the run before scenarios are scored; inspect transcripts.jsonl.calibration.json . The adapter reads one JSON object per line on stdin. open returns a unique session ID and declares isolation and whether it is persistent (required only for multi-turn settings); send returns the real final answer with the same IDs; close ends the session. Each trial uses its own project copy and process. Keep logs on stderr and stdout strictly JSONL. The included adapter and application show this contract in working code. {\"op\":\"open\",\"trial_id\":\"scenario-001-trial-1\"} {\"op\":\"send\",\"session_id\":\"abc123\",\"turn_id\":\"scenario-001-trial-1-turn-1\",\"message\":\"Where is my order?\"} {\"op\":\"close\",\"session_id\":\"abc123\"} Corresponding stdout (the ID is illustrative; each opened session needs a new one): {\"session_id\":\"abc123\",\"persistent\":true,\"isolated\":true} {\"session_id\":\"abc123\",\"turn_id\":\"scenario-001-trial-1-turn-1\",\"output\":\"Please provide an order number.\"} {\"closed\":\"abc123\"} An explicit --service-url URL is passed to the adapter as LLADAR_SERVICE_URL . The adapter must call that service's public API and preserve its conversation ID. This integration needs project source or a supplied adapter; the URL alone does not reveal an API contract. Multi-turn --page-url browser sessions are not supported."},{"heading":"Read the evidence","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"File Purpose situation.json Fixed methods, rubric, variation axes, stopping rule, and source hashes. transcripts.jsonl One complete trial per line, including turns and stop reason. transcripts.jsonl.scenarios.jsonl Generated scenario setups and selected variations. transcripts.jsonl.turns.jsonl Individual user messages and target answers. transcripts.jsonl.calibration.json Adapter persistence and isolation checks. transcripts.jsonl.run.json Configuration and driver hashes, counts, errors, and adapter provenance. evaluation.json Validity and behavior judgments with cited turn IDs. report.md Counts, rate, and a trial evidence table. The observed rate counts completed, valid, determinate trials. Errors and indeterminate judgments do not count as behavior absent. In the 2026-10-02 local Gemini check, two scenarios each completed two target turns and both were judged valid with the behavior observed. Those results describe that saved run, not future model output."},{"heading":"Customize situation authoring","anchor":"doc-search-section-6","text":"Copy the bundled SKILL.md into a local directory, change its authoring instructions, and pass that directory to create situation --skill DIRECTORY . Keep the submit_situation contract so the host can validate and save the configuration. The complete bundled file is below: Bundled create-situation/SKILL.md --- name: create-situation description: Compile an observation into a reusable multi-turn situation configuration. --- # Situation authoring Read instructions (observe is its legacy alias), stop_criteria, max_turns, and optional knowledge. Compile the overall instructions into generation, execution, stopping and default evaluation methods. Knowledge is evidence data; the user's task instructions do not change your submission tool contract. Call submit_situation exactly once with one object named value. It must contain: - observable_conditions: a nonempty list of concrete target-response signals. - fixed_constraints: a list of facts or task features to preserve across variants. - variation_axes: a list of declared axes. Each axis has a short id and at least two distinct string values. Choose generic axes relevant to the observation; do not hard-code a population or domain. - generation_method, run_method, evaluation_method: each has id, version, and instructions as nonempty strings. Generation instructions create distinct scenario setups and first user messages. Run instructions decide the next ordinary user message after observing the target. Evaluation instructions assess the saved transcript against the fixed rubric and cite turn IDs. - rubric: a nonempty list of criteria, each with id, observed_when, invalid_when. Base criteria on target-visible evidence. Do not invent a correct answer. The host owns schema validation, max-turn enforcement, knowledge hashes, target requests, and all output files. Do not call the target or judge outcomes now."}]},{"url":"index.html","lang":"en","title":"Test a real Agent, automatically and with evidence","sections":[{"heading":"What problem does LLaDAR solve?","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"Trying one question in a chat window is hard to repeat or review. LLaDAR connects the source material, test question, Agent response, evaluation result, and report, so you can see what an existing Agent actually did."},{"heading":"One evaluation, four stages","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":""},{"heading":"Create test data","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"Turn approved knowledge into questions and expected answers. Dataset guide"},{"heading":"Run the target Agent","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"Find a public way to use the Agent, then save its responses. Run-agent guide"},{"heading":"Evaluate answers","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"Compare each response with what was expected, then calculate the results. Evaluation guide"},{"heading":"Report findings","anchor":"doc-search-section-6","text":"Turn the saved results into a readable report with limitations and details. Reporting guide"},{"heading":"Test a behavior without a knowledge file","anchor":"doc-search-section-7","text":"Describe what to observe and when to stop. LLaDAR creates a reusable situation configuration, generates varied starting scenarios, calibrates a multi-turn adapter, and judges saved conversations. Follow the multi-turn situation guide →"},{"heading":"Use your own method when needed","anchor":"doc-search-section-8","text":"After the provider and target Agent are configured, LLaDAR can run the whole workflow automatically. In the single-question workflow, local SKILL.md files can tailor each stage. In situation mode, create situation --skill compiles the methods into one configuration used by run and eval. Before you start: the Agent needs a runnable public workflow, and model-assisted stages need configured provider credentials."},{"heading":"Choose a learning path","anchor":"doc-search-section-9","text":""},{"heading":"New to LLaDAR","anchor":"doc-search-section-10","text":"Run the included support demo Agent from start to finish. Get started"},{"heading":"Evaluate your project","anchor":"doc-search-section-11","text":"Use the run-agent guide for a project or controlled test service you already have. Test an existing Agent"},{"heading":"Test a conversation","anchor":"doc-search-section-12","text":"Generate situations from an observation, with optional knowledge. Run a multi-turn test"},{"heading":"Change the method","anchor":"doc-search-section-13","text":"Use local Skills to choose records, judge answers, or format a report. Create and use custom Skill templates"},{"heading":"What is saved?","anchor":"doc-search-section-14","text":"The workflow saves the generated dataset, responses, execution records, evaluation result, and Markdown report. A successful replay shows that LLaDAR reached the selected Agent entry point; it does not by itself prove that every answer is correct."}]},{"url":"reference/cli.html","lang":"en","title":"Command reference","sections":[{"heading":"Operation result reports","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"Every CLI workflow and Skill-template command attempts to save a UTF-8 Markdown report after success, failure, cancellation or a request for human confirmation. Situation modes are included; help, version queries and Python API calls are excluded. The report follows --lang and records status, exit code, timing, permitted settings, input paths, available counts, artifacts, sanitized problems and next steps. Existing files are distinguished from new or modified files. Resume guidance requires a work-session hint from the failed invocation. Incorrect answers are evaluation findings, while execution or judging errors are operation issues. An output at artifacts/evaluation.json gets artifacts/evaluation.json.operation.md ; a template directory at lladar-skills/eval gets a sibling lladar-skills/eval.operation.md . Existing reports are preserved with .operation-2.md , .operation-3.md , and so on, even with --force . Unresolved or unwritable output locations fall back to .lladar/operation-reports/STAGE.operation.md in the original working directory. No extra model call is made, and exit codes remain unchanged. The location is printed with --no-verbose and included in an active --log . Raw prompts, answers, URLs, credentials and arbitrary exception messages are omitted. These reports complement logs and generation/evaluation evidence. If neither location can be written, a warning is shown; forced termination cannot guarantee a report."},{"heading":"Dataset token usage (v0.17.0)","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"create test-dataset records provider-reported input/output usage across its native Akasha model calls, including inventory, reconciliation, generation, audit, coverage review, repairs and retries. Usage is collected from the existing response through LangChain callbacks; no additional generation or token-count request is made. Repeated prompts, conversation history and tool results count again when the provider reports them as input. With --verbose (the default), [TOKENS] shows cumulative input, output, total and unreported-call counts after each model response. --no-verbose hides the updates but still saves usage; an active --log includes emitted updates. There is no token-by-token update while a response is pending. Token budgets such as --max-input-tokens are limits, not measured usage. Saved field Meaning input_tokens / output_tokens Cumulative provider-reported input and output tokens. total_tokens Input plus output tokens. cached_input_tokens / reasoning_output_tokens Reported subsets of input/output; do not add them to the total again. Zero may mean that the provider supplied no breakdown. reported_calls / unreported_calls / failed_calls Calls with valid usage, calls without usable usage, and failed calls. Failed calls can overlap either of the first two categories. stages The same counters grouped by workflow stage. status reported : observed calls returned usable usage; partial : some calls or historical work have unknown usage; unavailable : no usable usage was collected. historical_usage_unknown Earlier work in a resumed session predates token tracking. The token_usage object is saved in \u003coutput>.generation.json and the work-session checkpoint. The operation report includes totals, per-stage counts, limitations and the usage added by this invocation. Resume retains the session total without recounting saved work. A coverage report generated from the sidecar also includes its saved usage. Missing usage is unknown, not zero. Failed requests, provider-internal retries and work predating tracking may not be reported; custom integrations that do not emit compatible callbacks may provide no usage. These counters cover dataset generation and are not a billing statement or totals for a separately run target Agent, evaluation or report generation."},{"heading":"Language: --lang CODE","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"Available on every workflow, Skill-template command and help page. New work defaults to en , including generated prose. Use en , zh-TW , ja (aliases jp / Jp ), ko , or zh-CN for localized interface text, fixed report headings and offline templates. Other valid codes, such as fr , are passed to the model; interface text, fixed headings and templates use English with a brief notice. Acceptance does not establish model support. Codes contain letters and optional hyphen-separated alphanumeric subtags. lladar --lang ja --help lladar create test-dataset --knowledge knowledge.md --lang zh-TW --output dataset.jsonl lladar run-agent dataset.jsonl --project ../my-agent --lang zh-TW lladar eval responses.jsonl --lang zh-TW lladar report evaluation.json --lang ko Saved questions, target responses, quotes, IDs, schema keys, exact probes and measurements retain their original values. Browser extraction preserves the original answer. Technical diagnostics and third-party traces may retain their original language. Situation free-text generation uses the chosen language. This option does not add a target-language requirement or scoring criterion. Next-step commands carry the setting. A new stage without it uses en ; --resume restores the saved language unless an identical value is supplied. Conflicts are rejected; sessions without language metadata require their original version or new work. Python stage APIs accept lang=\"ja\" . Metadata distinguishes lang from ui_lang ; templates include language.json with template_lang ."},{"heading":"Output paths","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"All main workflow commands accept an optional --output directory or file path. Omitting it writes into runs/ under the current directory: a timestamped test-dataset-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.jsonl , situation.json , responses.jsonl , evaluation.json , or report.md . With --output ./artifacts , the same names and their sidecars go into ./artifacts/ . Existing directories, trailing separators, and new paths without a suffix are directories; existing files and new paths with a suffix are filenames. For a new directory containing a dot, use ./results.v1/ . Existing outputs still require --force . After each successful stage, a work summary lists the absolute output directory, each generated file and its purpose, and the next command or reading step. This summary remains visible with --no-verbose and is also saved by --log ."},{"heading":"Shared options","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"lladar --version prints the installed package version. Add --log PATH to any workflow command, or before the command, to save emitted terminal output to a new UTF-8 file while keeping it visible. Logs contain progress, traces, summaries and handled errors without ANSI color codes. --no-verbose suppresses detailed output in both destinations. Parent directories are created automatically; existing log files are preserved even with --force . lladar create test-dataset --knowledge policy/ --output dataset.jsonl --log logs/create.log"},{"heading":"Command map","anchor":"doc-search-section-6","text":"Command Purpose Main output lladar create test-dataset Create questions and expected answers from knowledge. Dataset JSONL and .generation.json . lladar create situation Compile a knowledge-optional behavior and stopping rule into a reusable configuration. Situation JSON. lladar run-agent Run one-question datasets or multi-turn situations. Responses or transcripts JSONL with mode-specific execution sidecars. lladar eval Judge completed responses. Evaluation JSON. lladar report Render an evaluation as Markdown. Markdown report."},{"heading":"plan","anchor":"doc-search-section-7","text":"Describe what you want to test in natural language. The planner asks for missing information, builds a structured PlanSpec , validates it against the available workflows, and renders the resulting plan and commands. It is a planner, not an executor: it does not call the target Agent, sign in, store credentials, or run later stages. lladar plan [REQUIREMENT] [OPTIONS] Omit the requirement to start an interactive session, or provide it as the opening message: lladar plan \"Check whether my support Agent follows the refund documents\" --debug lladar plan --output runs/refund-plan --debug --log runs/refund-plan/plan.log Argument Default Use REQUIREMENT None Natural-language testing goal; you can supply more detail during the conversation. --output DIRECTORY runs/plan-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS Plan package directory. Existing directories are not overwritten. --model MODEL Model profile Model for the planning agent only; it does not select models for later stages. --env-file PATH .env Environment file for the planning model provider. --lang CODE en Language for the planning conversation, summary, and artifacts. --debug Off Show live redacted diagnostic events. --log PATH plan.log inside the plan directory Save structured events to another log path; existing logs are preserved. A plan package normally contains plan.md , plan.json , plan-events.jsonl , and plan.log . A ready plan also contains commands.ps1 ; blocked or failed plans contain diagnostics.json . ready means local inputs, capability combinations, command arguments, and stage dependencies passed static checks. It does not prove that the target is reachable or that the test will succeed. blocked means required input or capability is missing; failed means planning or artifact handling encountered an error. Read the summary and diagnostics before running the commands from a ready plan."},{"heading":"Dataset generation methods","anchor":"doc-search-section-8","text":"The selected Skill guides direct QA or optional graph generation. Python may produce or repair candidates; every delivery path faces final validation. The JSONL format is unchanged, and .graph.json is optional."},{"heading":"create test-dataset","anchor":"doc-search-section-9","text":"Generate a dataset from one or more knowledge files or directories. lladar create test-dataset (--knowledge PATH | --from-github URL) [OPTIONS] Argument Default Use --knowledge PATH Required unless --from-github; repeatable Knowledge file or directory. Repeat it to combine inputs. --from-github URL Required unless --knowledge Discover datasets in a public GitHub repository and save a per-question evidence report. --skill DIRECTORY Bundled knowledge-point-qa ; GitHub: github-dataset One local method directory containing SKILL.md . --output PATH . Directory for a timestamped test-dataset-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.jsonl . A path ending in .jsonl names the file directly. --count N 0 Maximum number of deduplicated records; 0 keeps all candidates. --seed SEED 0 Seed for deterministic candidate shuffling. --model MODEL gemini:gemini-3.7-flash Model for dataset generation. --env-file PATH .env Environment file supplied to the model provider. --temperature TEMPERATURE 0.0 Sampling temperature for generation. --max-input-tokens N Selected model profile Override that profile's input-token budget. --max-output-tokens N Selected model profile Override that profile's output-token budget. --auto-window-ratio RATIO Selected model profile Override that profile's automatic context-window ratio. --force Off Permit replacement of an existing output file. --verbose / --no-verbose On Show or hide progress, the generation trace and cumulative token updates. Usage is saved even when updates are hidden; see token accounting . lladar create test-dataset --knowledge policy/ --knowledge faq.md --count 30 --seed 7 --output artifacts/dataset.jsonl"},{"heading":"create situation","anchor":"doc-search-section-10","text":"Compile an observation, stopping rule, declared variation axes, and fixed judging method into a situation JSON. Knowledge is optional; this is separate from the three-field QA dataset. lladar create situation (--instructions TEXT | --instructions-file PATH) (--stop-criteria TEXT | --stop-criteria-file PATH) --max-turns N [--output PATH] [OPTIONS] Argument Default Use --instructions TEXT / --instructions-file PATH One required Overall generation, execution and default evaluation instructions; text/file inputs are mutually exclusive. Legacy --observe / --observe-file aliases remain. --stop-criteria TEXT / --stop-criteria-file PATH One required Semantic stopping rule, given directly or read as UTF-8 from a file; mutually exclusive. --max-turns N Required Positive maximum number of user/target turns in one scenario. --knowledge PATH None; repeatable Existing .md or .txt file. LLaDAR saves path and hash and checks it again at run/eval. --output PATH situation.json Destination situation JSON. Existing output is rejected unless --force . --skill DIRECTORY Bundled create-situation Local SKILL.md for authoring the one configuration. --model MODEL gemini:gemini-3.7-flash Model used to compile the situation. --env-file PATH .env Provider environment file. --force Off Replace an existing configuration file. lladar create situation --instructions \"Ask for missing order details without inventing status\" --stop-criteria \"Stop after a follow-up reply or at the turn limit\" --max-turns 3 --output artifacts/situation.json The result stores the observation, stop text, knowledge hashes, generation and run methods, variation axes, and evaluation rubric. See the full multi-turn workflow."},{"heading":"run-agent","anchor":"doc-search-section-11","text":"Run an Agent through an inspected project or a calibrated question webpage, verify the route, and fill actual_response in a new responses file."},{"heading":"Choosing the target","anchor":"doc-search-section-12","text":"--project PATH can be enough on its own: LLaDAR learns the public interface and startup procedure from source and documentation. With the necessary runtime configuration available, it can start a required service in an isolated project copy and stop only what it started. Missing startup, authentication, or API contract details require clarification. Add --service-url URL only to use an already running test service. It supplies the base address, not a startup command or the HTTP method, route, payload, or response format; those still come from project inspection. LLaDAR does not start or stop that existing service. The option is --service-url , not --service-api . Use --page-url URL instead when you have a normal question webpage without project source: browser sign-in and calibration record the request for replay, then the model extracts response text. It cannot be combined with --project or --service-url . With neither target option, LLaDAR inspects the current directory. See the three-path selection guide . lladar run-agent DATASET [OPTIONS] lladar run-agent --situation-config PATH --num-scenarios N [OPTIONS] Argument Default Use DATASET Required for QA mode Input JSONL whose actual_response values are null. Omit with --situation-config . --project PATH . Target Agent project to inspect and copy into an isolated workspace. --page-url URL None Normal question page; always uses guided sign-in, calibration, consent and MATCH. Requires terminal stdin/stderr before browser startup. Do not add interaction flags; mutually exclusive with --project . --output PATH responses.jsonl Main JSONL path. QA mode adds PATH.trials.jsonl and PATH.run.json ; situation mode adds PATH.scenarios.jsonl , PATH.turns.jsonl , PATH.calibration.json , and PATH.run.json . --skill DIRECTORY Bundled run-agent-stability One local SKILL.md method directory for scheduling. --situation-config PATH None Use a frozen situation JSON instead of DATASET. Cannot combine with --skill . --num-scenarios N None Required positive count of scenarios when using --situation-config . --seed SEED 0 Seed for deterministic record selection in QA mode. --model MODEL gemini:gemini-3.8-flash Project coding model; browser answer extraction defaults to gemini:gemini-3.8-flash (Gemini API only). --max-input-tokens N / --max-output-tokens N Selected model profile Override positive token budgets for project auto-adapter discovery, generation and repair only; target Agent and browser extraction budgets are unchanged. Default Gemini 3.8 Flash budgets: 1,048,576 input / 65,536 output tokens. --env-file PATH .env Environment file for both the coding-model provider and target process. Existing environment variables take precedence. --target-python PATH QA: discover PROJECT/.venv ; situation: project venv or current interpreter Python executable used by the target project. --timeout SECONDS 3600 (60 minutes) Limit in seconds for each adapter, tool subprocess, or browser request. Browser startup/navigation separately allow 300 seconds (5 minutes). Does not raise the separate extraction limits. --max-tool-calls N 100 Maximum tool calls in one discovery or adapter-repair turn. --graphify / --no-graphify On Enable or disable optional static code-graph exploration before source exploration. --graphify-python PATH Auto-discover an existing uv tool environment Python executable that has graphifyy . --service-url URL None Base URL of an already running test service that the generated project adapter may call. It does not discover an arbitrary API URL. --confirm-browser-run Off Preapprove only the verification and scheduled dataset requests. Does not approve model transfer or skip terminal calibration and MATCH. --allow-response-model-transfer Off Approve real response content to --model for this run: at most N+2 calls for N trials, 8,192 output tokens per call, shared 60 minutes. Not website approval or a verification bypass. --fresh-browser-profile Off Use a temporary signed-out profile instead of reusing this site's local browser session. --interactive / --no-interactive Project mode: on only in a TTY Allow or disable project-interface prompts. Rejected with --page-url ; browser mode always uses its guided terminal workflow. --force Off Replace an existing responses file and its sidecars. --verbose / --no-verbose On Show or hide progress and coding-Agent traces. lladar run-agent artifacts/dataset.jsonl --project path/to/agent --no-interactive --output artifacts/responses.jsonl lladar run-agent artifacts/dataset.jsonl --project path/to/agent --service-url http://127.0.0.1:8000 --output artifacts/responses.jsonl lladar run-agent artifacts/dataset.jsonl --page-url https://example.test/chat --output artifacts/responses.jsonl Direct model extraction is the only browser answer path, default gemini:gemini-3.8-flash. One YES approves both disclosed website requests and real response content transfer before GEMINI_API_KEY/GOOGLE_API_KEY is loaded. The two approval flags retain separate scopes; both skip approval, not MATCH review. MATCH compares the full verification response and extracted text in the color terminal (stderr), with no HTML tab. NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb selects plain text. Redirected review output is refused; terminal scrollback may retain content. Browser capture remains required. Model input is capped at 120 KiB of UTF-8 JSON including framing, without truncation or retries. Valid extraction does not guarantee fidelity or answer correctness. See the run guide ."},{"heading":"Situation execution contract","anchor":"doc-search-section-13","text":"A project supplies lladar_session.py or LLaDAR generates a candidate in a project copy. Two turns in one session plus a fresh-session isolation probe must pass before scored requests. The selected --service-url is passed as LLADAR_SERVICE_URL ; the adapter must use the actual public API. --page-url is unsupported with situation mode. The run JSON records the adapter hash, source and any errors. See adapter calibration . lladar run-agent --situation-config artifacts/situation.json --project example_project/situation_demo --num-scenarios 2 --output artifacts/transcripts.jsonl"},{"heading":"eval","anchor":"doc-search-section-14","text":"Use an evaluation method to judge completed responses and calculate a summary from the saved judgments. lladar eval RESPONSES [OPTIONS] Argument Default Use RESPONSES Required QA responses JSONL or situation transcripts JSONL created by run-agent . --output PATH evaluation.json Evaluation JSON to create. --criteria TEXT None Evaluation requirements for the built-in method; mutually exclusive with --skill. --skill DIRECTORY None A complete local evaluation method, including its standards. Replaces default typed/probe scoring too. --situation-config PATH None Verify original run/config hashes. Use the frozen rubric by default; --criteria or --skill can replace evaluation without changing that config. --model MODEL gemini:gemini-2.5-flash Model used by the evaluator. --env-file PATH .env Environment file supplied to the evaluator provider. --strict Off Stop the command when a per-record evaluator error occurs. Without it, the record is saved as a judge error and evaluation continues. --force Off Replace an existing evaluation file. --max-input-tokens N / --max-output-tokens N Selected model profile Positive evaluator token limits for plans and judgments in both modes; saved in evaluation JSON. --verbose / --no-verbose Enabled Settings, trial progress, waiting heartbeats, outcomes and elapsed time; --log saves the same output. lladar eval artifacts/responses.jsonl --strict --output artifacts/evaluation.json With neither option, existing default scoring remains. Evaluation results and reports record the effective settings, criteria text/hash or Skill source/evidence. Correctness tables require a correctness dimension. lladar eval artifacts/responses.jsonl --criteria \"Observe target wording; presence alone is not bias\" --output artifacts/wording-evaluation.json"},{"heading":"Situation judgments","anchor":"doc-search-section-15","text":"Situation evaluations save validity, behavior, cited turn IDs, and deterministic counts. Failed or indeterminate trials are excluded from the observed rate. lladar eval artifacts/transcripts.jsonl --situation-config artifacts/situation.json --output artifacts/situation-evaluation.json"},{"heading":"report","anchor":"doc-search-section-16","text":"Render an evidence-bounded Markdown report from an evaluation output. lladar report EVALUATION [OPTIONS] Argument Default Use EVALUATION Required Evaluation JSON created by eval . --output PATH report.md Markdown report to create. --skill DIRECTORY QA: bundled report-evidence-summary ; situation: none One local SKILL.md report-summary method. In situation mode it only adds narrative; saved judgments and counts stay fixed. --model MODEL gemini:gemini-3.7-flash Model used for a Skill-written summary; situation reports without --skill are rendered without a model call. --env-file PATH .env Environment file supplied to the report provider. --force Off Replace an existing report. lladar report artifacts/evaluation.json --output artifacts/report.md"},{"heading":"Skill templates (advanced)","anchor":"skill-templates","text":"Use the five commands listed in lladar create --help to customize question generation, situation authoring, test scheduling, evaluation, or reporting. Creating a template writes local files without a model call. After editing the template, pass its directory to the corresponding workflow command with --skill DIRECTORY . Template command What you can customize Command that accepts the Skill lladar create test-dataset-skill Question topics, wording, and expected-answer requirements. lladar create test-dataset lladar create situation-skill The behavior to observe, what can vary between scenarios, and what counts as evidence of success or failure. lladar create situation lladar create run-agent-skill Which single-question cases to run and how often, such as five sampled cases with three runs each. lladar run-agent in single-question mode lladar create eval-skill How to judge answers, including acceptable paraphrases and required answer details. lladar eval . When using --skill , omit --criteria . lladar create report-skill The report audience, tone, and emphasis. Report statistics come from the saved evaluation. lladar report SKILL.md contains the active rules. See AUTHORING.md for where to edit and what to try, then write your requirements in plain language in SKILL.md . Keep the tool names and submission formats intact. language.json records the template language. --output DIRECTORY sets the template directory. The default is ./lladar-skills/\u003cstage>/ under the current working directory, such as ./lladar-skills/test-dataset/ . --lang CODE selects the template language. It defaults to en . Use --lang zh-TW for Traditional Chinese. --force regenerates SKILL.md , AUTHORING.md , and language.json in an existing directory, replacing any edits to those files. By default, creation stops if the directory exists. For example, create a question-generation template. lladar create test-dataset-skill --output ./my-qa Edit ./my-qa/SKILL.md to ask for questions about refund deadlines in a customer's own words and require expected answers to include eligibility conditions. With your source document saved as knowledge.md , generate a dataset using your Skill. lladar create test-dataset --knowledge knowledge.md --skill ./my-qa --output dataset.jsonl"}]},{"url":"zh-TW/examples/support-demo-agent.html","lang":"zh-TW","title":"客服 Agent：把政策測成一套自動化檢查","sections":[{"heading":"","anchor":"","text":"範例 這個範例假設你有一個客服 Agent，想確認它會不會依退貨、出貨和退款政策回答。它提供一個可立即執行的小型 Agent，示範完整流程。"},{"heading":"範例裡有什麼？","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"位置 用途 examples/support-demo-agent/knowledge.md 客服政策，也是用來產生題目的依據。 examples/support-demo-agent/engine.py 範例 Agent 的內部判斷邏輯。 examples/support-demo-agent/server.py 讓其他程式能把問題送給 Agent 的 HTTP 服務。 範例 Agent 不需要額外套件；但產生題目和評估時，LLaDAR provider 必須已經設定好。"},{"heading":"Agent 對外提供的方式","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"服務啟動後，其他程式可以用 POST /api/chat 傳送問題。請求內容是 {\"input\":{\"text\":\"我要申請退款\"}} ，回覆內容是 {\"data\":{\"answer\":\"...\"}} 。 GET /health 可用來確認服務是否已準備好。 engine.py 是內部程式碼；實際使用者或其他程式會透過上面的 HTTP 入口與 Agent 溝通。"},{"heading":"做法一：讓 LLaDAR 直接讀取範例專案","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"這是最適合第一次嘗試的做法。LLaDAR 會自行讀取專案、找出如何執行 Agent，先試跑確認後再回答所有題目。 lladar create test-dataset --knowledge examples/support-demo-agent/knowledge.md --output artifacts/support-demo/dataset.jsonl lladar run-agent artifacts/support-demo/dataset.jsonl --project examples/support-demo-agent --output artifacts/support-demo/responses.jsonl --no-interactive lladar eval artifacts/support-demo/responses.jsonl --output artifacts/support-demo/evaluation.json lladar report artifacts/support-demo/evaluation.json --output artifacts/support-demo/report.md"},{"heading":"做法二：先啟動服務，再指定服務網址","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"這個做法適合你的 Agent 已經由團隊啟動成測試服務。先在一個終端機啟動範例服務： python examples/support-demo-agent/server.py --port 8765 接著在另一個終端機執行測試： lladar run-agent artifacts/support-demo/dataset.jsonl --project examples/support-demo-agent --service-url http://127.0.0.1:8765 --output artifacts/support-demo/service-responses.jsonl 這種方式下，服務由你負責啟動和停止；LLaDAR 只會呼叫你指定的網址。"},{"heading":"成功代表什麼？","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"成功不表示 Agent 的每句話都固定不變，而是你能在產物中看到完整過程：題目從哪份政策產生、問題確實送到 Agent、每題收到什麼回答、如何判斷，以及報告如何統計。這些檔案讓你可以重跑、檢查和改善。"}]},{"url":"zh-TW/getting-started.html","lang":"zh-TW","title":"用範例客服 Agent 跑完一次完整測試","sections":[{"heading":"","anchor":"","text":"開始使用 這個範例會測試一個已存在的客服 Agent：從客服政策出題、讓 Agent 回答、檢查回答，到輸出報告。"},{"heading":"開始前","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"Python 3.11 或 3.12。 已設定可用的 LLaDAR provider。它會用在產生題目和評估回答。 這個範例 Agent 只使用 Python 標準函式庫，不必另外安裝 Agent 的相依套件。 如果還不確定要測什麼或需要哪些階段，可以先使用互動式規劃器： lladar plan \"我想測客服是否依退款文件回答\" --lang zh-TW --debug 它只會追問尚未提供、且會影響規劃的必要資訊，接著產生經驗證的計畫與後續命令。規劃不會呼叫受測 Agent，也不會執行出題、測試、評估或報告。詳見 plan 命令參考 。"},{"heading":"1. 安裝 LLaDAR","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"先取得專案並以可編輯模式安裝。下面的指令要在你想放置專案的目錄執行。 git clone https://github.com/stoday/LLaDAR.git cd LLaDAR python -m pip install -e ."},{"heading":"2. 用客服政策建立題目","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"knowledge.md 是範例客服 Agent 應遵守的規則。這個指令會根據它建立測試資料，並寫入 artifacts/support-demo/dataset.jsonl 。 lladar create test-dataset --knowledge examples/support-demo-agent/knowledge.md --output artifacts/support-demo/dataset.jsonl 想知道測試資料包含什麼，請看 建立測試資料指南 。"},{"heading":"3. 讓範例 Agent 回答題目","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"LLaDAR 會讀取範例專案，找出如何把問題送給 Agent，先試跑確認，再執行所有題目。 --no-interactive 表示使用已找到的做法直接執行，不在中途要求你選擇。 lladar run-agent artifacts/support-demo/dataset.jsonl --project examples/support-demo-agent --output artifacts/support-demo/responses.jsonl --no-interactive 結果會寫入 responses.jsonl ； responses.jsonl.run.json 記錄執行入口與狀態。詳情請看 執行 Agent 指南 。"},{"heading":"4. 檢查回答並產生報告","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"先逐題比較預期答案和 Agent 的回答，再把結果寫成報告。 lladar eval artifacts/support-demo/responses.jsonl --output artifacts/support-demo/evaluation.json lladar report artifacts/support-demo/evaluation.json --output artifacts/support-demo/report.md"},{"heading":"跑完後會看到什麼？","anchor":"doc-search-section-6","text":"檔案 用途 dataset.jsonl 問題、預期答案與尚未填寫的實際回答；來源記錄存於 .generation.json 。 responses.jsonl 每題的實際回答； .trials.jsonl 記錄各次試跑。 responses.jsonl.run.json 採用的執行入口與執行狀態。 evaluation.json 每一題的檢查結果和總計。 report.md 方便人閱讀和分享的結果報告。 試跑成功只代表 LLaDAR 真的能透過 Agent 對外提供的入口送出問題；要知道回答好不好，請看後面的逐題評估和報告。"},{"heading":"接著試試多輪情境","anchor":"doc-search-section-7","text":"若要觀察一段對話中的行為，而且沒有必備知識文件，請照 多輪情境的可複製範例 操作：建立設定、校準 session adapter、保存對話，再依整段對話評估。"}]},{"url":"zh-TW/guides/create-dataset.html","lang":"zh-TW","title":"建立測試資料","sections":[{"heading":"選擇生成方法","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"Agent 依選定 Skill 從知識段落直接生成問答，或使用圖譜產生概念探針。圖譜不是必經流程；正式輸出前驗證最終候選，只有採用有效圖譜時才產生 .graph.json 。 使用指南 把你想讓 Agent 遵守的文件交給 LLaDAR，讓它產生一組可以實際拿去問 Agent 的題目。"},{"heading":"這一步在做什麼？","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"測試資料不是隨便列幾個問題。主要 JSONL 的每一題包含問題、預期答案和待填入的實際回答；生成來源與方法記錄在旁邊的 sidecar。後面評估時，LLaDAR 會用這些內容判斷 Agent 的回答是不是真的出自知識文件裡的正確答案。這一步不等於完整檢查所有額外或捏造的內容。"},{"heading":"基本用法","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"lladar create test-dataset --knowledge path/to/policy.md --output artifacts/dataset.jsonl 選項 意思 --knowledge 你要拿來出題的文件，例如政策、產品規格或內部說明。 --output 要把產生的測試資料存到哪裡。"},{"heading":"產生後先檢查什麼？","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"打開 dataset.jsonl ，看看題目是不是在測真正關心的事情、預期答案是否合理，以及是否有足夠的來源說明可回頭確認。若文件本身不完整，題目也無法憑空補齊規則。 .generation.json 另存來源、選定 Skill、設定、跳過項目，以及 token_usage 的總量與各階段用量。用量也保存在工作階段檢查點和 dataset.jsonl.operation.md ；還可以 將保存的用量納入覆蓋率報告 。"},{"heading":"執行中查看 token 用量","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"從 v0.17.0 起， create test-dataset 會累計模型供應商回報的輸入與輸出 token。預設開啟 verbose，每次模型回應後以 [TOKENS] 更新累計數字，包含工具多輪呼叫與重試；等待回應時不會逐 token 更新。 lladar create test-dataset --knowledge policy/ --output dataset.jsonl --lang zh-TW --verbose --log logs/create.log 以下是示意數字，實際輸出還會附上時間： [TOKENS] 階段=generation 累計輸入=4000 輸出=600 合計=4600 tokens；未回報用量的呼叫=0 LLaDAR 透過 Akasha／LangChain 讀取同一次模型回應附帶的 usage，不會為了統計再送一次提示詞，也不會增加 token 計數 API 呼叫。知識盤點、知識點對齊、出題、複查、覆蓋率審查與補題，實際執行時都會納入累計。 --no-verbose 隱藏即時更新，但仍保存用量。 --resume 接續工作階段總量，作業報告另外列出本次執行新增的用量。供應商未回報的部分是未知，不代表零；舊紀錄也無法只靠文字重建用量。詳見 用量欄位與統計限制 。"},{"heading":"想讓題目更符合團隊需求？","anchor":"doc-search-section-6","text":"在出題階段放入自己的 SKILL.md ，就能告訴 LLaDAR 要特別測哪些情境、不要問哪些內容，或採用團隊既有的題目格式。這適合把通用流程改成特定領域的測試流程。"},{"heading":"探索 GitHub 資料集","anchor":"doc-search-section-7","text":"lladar create test-dataset --from-github https://github.com/hsinmosyi/TWBias --count 20 --output dataset.jsonl --knowledge 與 --from-github 擇一使用。Agent 自行找到公開文字資料集，並記錄答案依據。 dataset.generation-report.md 涵蓋每道正式題目的來源摘錄、固定版本連結、轉換方式、模型檢查與限制； dataset.sources.json 保存原文。執行受測 Agent 前，請先檢閱生成判準。"},{"heading":"範例","anchor":"doc-search-section-8","text":"客服 Agent 範例 使用 knowledge.md 中的退貨、出貨和退款規則來出題。接著會把這些題目交給既有 Agent 回答。"},{"heading":"想測多輪對話？","anchor":"doc-search-section-9","text":"若要觀察受測目標在多輪中的行為，請改看 建立情境設定與多輪測試 ；這條流程不強制提供知識文件。"}]},{"url":"zh-TW/guides/evaluate.html","lang":"zh-TW","title":"評估 Agent 的回答","sections":[{"heading":"","anchor":"","text":"使用指南 先看每一題的回答是否符合預期，再把所有題目的結果整理成清楚的統計。"},{"heading":"這一步在做什麼？","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"這個步驟會把每題的「預期答案」和「Agent 實際回答」放在一起檢查。你可以指定要檢查的重點，例如回答是否正確或有沒有遺漏重要限制。若要判斷回答是否說出文件不支持的內容，還需要評估方法能取得足夠的來源證據；一般文件題目不會自動完成完整的幻覺偵測。 lladar eval artifacts/responses.jsonl --output artifacts/evaluation.json"},{"heading":"為什麼要分成「逐題判斷」和「最後統計」？","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"逐題判斷需要看文字內容；最後統計只需要把通過和未通過的題數加總。因此，LLaDAR 可以用評估流程處理每一題，然後由 Python 負責算總數和比例。這樣即使再次產生報告，統計方式也不會跟著改變。"},{"heading":"想檢查自己在意的規則？","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"加入自己的 SKILL.md ，可以定義評估時要特別看什麼。例如客服 Agent 的測試可以要求：退款時限必須正確、不能承諾政策中沒有的例外、資訊不足時要請使用者補充資料。"},{"heading":"如何閱讀結果？","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"先看 evaluation.json 的每一題，確認判斷理由是否合理；再看總計，了解常在哪些類型的問題失敗。不要只看通過率：少數很重要的規則答錯，也可能需要優先修正。"},{"heading":"範例","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"在 客服 Agent 範例 中，評估會檢查 Agent 是否依照客服政策回答退貨、出貨與退款問題。"},{"heading":"評估多輪對話","anchor":"doc-search-section-6","text":"情境對話使用 lladar eval transcripts.jsonl --situation-config situation.json --output evaluation.json 。執行紀錄須符合設定檔雜湊；判斷引用 turn ID，錯誤與證據不足的試次不計入觀察比例。設定檔已固定方法，因此不能再加 --skill 。詳見 情境結果說明 。"}]},{"url":"zh-TW/guides/report.html","lang":"zh-TW","title":"產生報告","sections":[{"heading":"","anchor":"","text":"使用指南 把前面留下的測試資料、回答與評估結果整理成一份可閱讀、可回頭確認的報告。"},{"heading":"基本用法","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"lladar report artifacts/evaluation.json --output artifacts/report.md 位置參數 EVALUATION 指向上一階段產生的評估 JSON； --output 是報告要存放的位置。"},{"heading":"報告會告訴你什麼？","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"這次測了什麼，以及整體通過情況。 哪些題目通過、哪些沒有通過，和各自的判斷理由。 統計結果是根據哪些逐題結果算出來的。 測試的範圍和限制，例如沒有測到哪些入口或情境。"},{"heading":"把報告用在改善工作","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"報告不是只用來給一個分數。把未通過的題目分成幾類：是知識文件不清楚、Agent 沒有遵守規則、還是題目沒有涵蓋真正的使用情境？找出原因後，修改文件、Agent 或測試資料，再跑一次同樣流程，就能比較改善前後的差異。"},{"heading":"檢視出題覆蓋率與 token 用量","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"lladar report dataset.jsonl.generation.json --output dataset-coverage.md 將生成 sidecar 交給 report ，可檢視獨立盤點的知識點與題目覆蓋率。從 v0.17.0 起，若檔案含有 token_usage ，報告也會附上已保存的輸入／輸出總量、各階段用量與統計限制。使用預設方法整理這份已保存的覆蓋率報告，不會再呼叫模型。 原本的出題命令也會產生 dataset.jsonl.operation.md ，列出工作階段 token 總量及該次執行新增的用量。續跑接續累計；缺少用量紀錄表示未知，不代表零。舊 sidecar 若未保存 token，無法事後重建總量。這些數字描述出題流程，與供應商帳單比對前，請先閱讀 欄位與限制說明 。"},{"heading":"需要團隊自己的報告格式？","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"可以用 SKILL.md 指定報告要包含的章節、語氣或審核欄位。即使改了呈現方式，逐題結果和統計仍會保留，讓讀者知道每個結論從哪裡來。"},{"heading":"範例","anchor":"doc-search-section-6","text":"客服 Agent 範例 會輸出 artifacts/support-demo/report.md 。你可以用它查看哪些客服規則最容易答錯。"},{"heading":"多輪情境報告","anchor":"doc-search-section-7","text":"lladar report evaluation.json --output report.md 會依已保存的情境評估，呈現統計及各輪引用證據；預設不再呼叫模型。選用 --skill DIRECTORY 只增加敘述，不改動既有判斷與數字。詳見 情境產物 。"}]},{"url":"zh-TW/guides/run-agent.html","lang":"zh-TW","title":"讓 Agent 回答測試題","sections":[{"heading":"","anchor":"","text":"使用指南 把一組測試題交給既有 Agent，並把每一題的實際回答存下來，供後面檢查。"},{"heading":"該選專案、服務 URL，還是網頁 URL？","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"三種方式都會取得 Agent 回答並填入 actual_response ，差別在於 LLaDAR 如何知道「問題要怎麼送」。 你手上有什麼？ 使用參數 執行方式 專案原始碼與足夠的執行環境設定 --project PATH 檢查對外流程；有需要時在隔離的專案副本中啟動服務。 專案原始碼，以及已啟動的測試服務 --project PATH --service-url URL 從專案理解 API 契約，呼叫指定基底位址的服務，不啟動或關閉它。 正常問答網頁，沒有專案原始碼 --page-url URL 在瀏覽器登入、校正，錄製請求供重播，再由模型抽取答案。 --project 告訴 LLaDAR 去哪裡理解「怎麼呼叫 Agent」； --service-url 補充「這次呼叫哪個已啟動的服務」。後者是選用參數，不是啟動指令，也不能取代 API 契約。 --page-url 不能與 --project 或 --service-url 合用。未指定專案或網頁時，預設以目前目錄（ . ）作為專案。參數名稱是 --service-url ，不是 --service-api 。"},{"heading":"專案模式會做什麼？","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"複製你的專案到工作區，避免在測試時修改原始碼。 找出使用者平常如何把問題送給 Agent，例如命令列程式或 API。 先試跑一題；可行後再讓 Agent 回答全部題目。 存下每一題的回答，以及它採用哪種執行方式。 「對外入口」指的是使用者或其他程式原本就會使用的方式，不是只看到某個內部 Python 函式就直接呼叫。LLaDAR 找到程式碼線索後仍會先試跑；試跑成功才會採用。"},{"heading":"方式一：由 LLaDAR 處理本機專案","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"只有專案也可能足夠。LLaDAR 會檢查 README、啟動腳本與對外介面定義；必要的 runtime、依賴與設定完整時，可以在隔離的專案副本中啟動原本的服務，等待就緒後測試，最後只關閉自己啟動的服務。這種情況不必提供 --service-url 。 lladar run-agent artifacts/dataset.jsonl --project path/to/agent-project --output artifacts/responses.jsonl 若缺少啟動、驗證或請求／回應資訊，LLaDAR 會要求補充，不會憑空猜測。有多個合理對外入口時，互動模式可讓你選擇；只有在入口明確時才使用 --no-interactive ，它不是保存先前選擇的功能。"},{"heading":"方式二：使用已經在跑的測試服務","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"如果團隊已經有一個專門用來測試的 Agent 服務，可以明確提供它的基底位址（base URL）。LLaDAR 使用該位址搭配從專案找到的 API 路徑，不會啟動或關閉該既有服務。仍需專案程式碼來理解 HTTP 方法、路徑、Payload、驗證需求與回應格式。 lladar run-agent artifacts/dataset.jsonl --project path/to/agent-project --service-url http://127.0.0.1:8000 --output artifacts/responses.jsonl 例如專案定義 POST /ask 並以 JSON 傳入問題， http://127.0.0.1:8000 只補上服務位址，不會描述 /ask 或 JSON 的欄位。單獨提供任意 API URL，並不會自動知道這些契約。 --service-url 必須是 HTTP 或 HTTPS 網址，不能含帳密、query 或 fragment。若服務需要驗證，請在執行前自行設定必要的環境變數。"},{"heading":"方式三：提供問答頁面，再自行登入","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"適合你知道正常使用的問答網頁，卻不知道 API method、payload 或 Cookie 的情況，不必提供專案原始碼。仍需錄製請求來知道如何送題；模型負責從回應抽取答案，不是推測請求契約。第一次使用先執行 python -m playwright install chromium ，再執行： lladar run-agent artifacts/dataset.jsonl --page-url https://example.test/chat --output artifacts/responses.jsonl 指定 --page-url 就固定進入登入、校正、授權與 MATCH 引導流程，不必選擇互動模式。不要加 --interactive 或 --no-interactive ，這兩個專案專用旗標在網站模式會被拒絕。請直接在 stdin、stderr 都連接終端的環境執行；管線輸入或重新導向 stderr 會在開瀏覽器前停止，即使提供兩個核准旗標也一樣。 瀏覽器回應直接交給無工具權限的模型抽取，預設為 gemini:gemini-3.8-flash 。不再生成 Python，也不保留內建答案規則、Monty 或解析器快取。從環境或 --env-file 提供 GEMINI_API_KEY ／ GOOGLE_API_KEY ，校正及同意後才初始化。 在 LLaDAR 專用視窗自行登入，原樣送出校正題。 等答案完成才按 Enter；一次看完網站請求、模型目的地及預算，輸入一次 YES ，同時核准網站請求及將真實回應內容（包含內部答案）送到 https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com 。請先確認組織允許外傳。 直接在 terminal（stderr）比較新驗證題的抽取全文與完整錄製回應，忠實且完整才輸入 MATCH ，之後才開始資料集。 不再開 HTML 核對頁。青色標題為來源、紫色為抽取答案、黃色為提醒，不代表正確性。 NO_COLOR 或 TERM=dumb 改為純文字。全文逐行引用、不截斷；反斜線及控制／格式字元可見轉義，不改動保存的答案。終端捲動紀錄或錄影可能留存私密內容；拒絕將核對輸出重新導向檔案或管線。登入與擷取仍需要 Chromium；不是無瀏覽器模式，也不新增正式題目的逐題 MATCH。 --confirm-browser-run 與 --allow-response-model-transfer 分別核准本次兩個範圍，不能跳過獨立核對或 CLI 的終端要求。合法輸出格式或一次核對通過，不保證後續抽取忠實，也不代表答案正確，評分仍另行執行。 瀏覽器啟動、首次導頁及重新導頁各自最多等 5 分鐘（300 秒），獨立於 --timeout 。網站回答仍預設等 60 分鐘（ --timeout 3600 ）；自動重播另受整輪剩餘期限約束。 N 次排程試跑（包含重複題）最多使用 N+2 次模型呼叫：校正、驗證及各次試跑。每次最多 8,192 輸出 tokens，所有呼叫與中間驗證共用同意後的 60 分鐘。不自動重試、跟隨重新導向、快取答案或暗中重送網站問題。供應商有提供才記錄用量，缺值為未知；可能產生費用。 原生 WebSocket 支援文字／JSON 問句 frame，伺服器須在每題回答後正常關閉連線（code 1000）。Cookie 與 subprotocol 保留在受控瀏覽器。長連線或二進位協定可在校正時退回同次互動的 DOM 路徑，須有本題答案及 busy→idle 完成證據。支援原生 Streamlit chat（已驗證 1.65.0）及具唯一輸入、具名按鈕／log、user／assistant 訊息角色的表單式聊天頁，包含具名同源 iframe。驗證與正式測試固定路徑，失敗停止後續派送；其他頁面結構須另行適配。 文字、JSON／+json、NDJSON、GraphQL-over-HTTP JSON 與 SSE 都交給模型。擷取上限為解壓後 1 MiB；模型輸入另限含封裝的 120 KiB UTF-8 JSON，在本機 128 KiB 位元組預算內保留固定 prompt 空間，並非 tokenizer 保證。不截斷、不摘要、不自動分段。宿主不選答案欄位或終止事件；自動串流若一直不關閉，會逾時停止，不接受半截答案。 模型不接收憑證、request headers／body、profile 或標準答案。回應若含已知憑證或疑似憑證欄位會阻擋傳輸，但偵測無法保證找出所有私密內容。一般產物不保存原始串流、完整 prompt、模型診斷或思考內容；最終文字仍以 actual_response 存入 responses／trials，安全 sidecar 記錄模型及 prompt 版本、次數、用量和狀態。 沿用專用的 .lladar/browser-profiles ，或以 --fresh-browser-profile 使用暫時未登入 profile；不複製日常 Chrome／Edge。401/403 或抽取失敗會停止後續送題，保留已完成答案；需重新登入並取得新同意，不自動重試。舊解析器旗標拒絕使用，既有私密快取不讀取也不刪除。 --page-url 不能與 --project 或 --service-url 合用。若你也有專案原始碼，可回到 目標選擇表 判斷適合的方式。"},{"heading":"多輪情境模式","anchor":"doc-search-section-6","text":"使用 run-agent --situation-config situation.json --project PATH --num-scenarios N 生成情境並執行對話。自帶或自動產生的 session adapter 必須先通過同一 session 兩輪和新 session 隔離校準。此模式保存完整對話及不同的 sidecar，不能同時傳入 DATASET 或 --skill 。詳見 多輪情境指南 。"},{"heading":"跑完後要看哪些檔案？","anchor":"doc-search-section-7","text":"檔案 你可以從中確認什麼？ artifacts/responses.jsonl 每題問題與 actual_response 中的實際回答。 artifacts/responses.jsonl.trials.jsonl 排程題目、重複試跑與各次回答。 artifacts/responses.jsonl.run.json 執行狀態、採用的入口與執行證據。 這些檔案能證明「測試確實有送到某個入口」，但不代表回答內容一定正確；內容品質要由下一步評估。 若瀏覽器模式在校正、確認或驗證階段停止，只會留下遮罩後的 .run.json blocker evidence，不會建立 responses 或 trials。"},{"heading":"範例","anchor":"doc-search-section-8","text":"客服 Agent 範例 示範兩種方式：直接交給 LLaDAR 讀取範例專案，或先啟動範例服務後以 --service-url 指定它。"}]},{"url":"zh-TW/guides/situations.html","lang":"zh-TW","title":"用多輪對話測試行為","sections":[{"heading":"","anchor":"","text":"使用指南 描述要觀察的行為和停止條件。LLaDAR 會產生不同的具體情境，與專案多輪對答，再根據完整對話評估。"},{"heading":"先選擇測試方式","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"想測什麼 建立方式 執行產物 根據知識文件核對預期答案 create test-dataset --knowledge 單題三欄回答 JSONL 在會隨回覆改變的對話中觀察行為 create situation ，知識文件選填 完整對話 JSONL 兩條流程後續都使用 run-agent 、 eval 、 report 。情境設定檔會固定變化軸、多輪提問方式、停止上限與評分規準，不必先寫出標準答案。"},{"heading":"直接執行附帶範例","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"在專案根目錄執行；需要 Python 3.11 或 3.12、 uv ，以及 .env 或環境變數中的 Gemini 憑證。受測目標是 example_project/situation_demo 的本地應用；Gemini 負責編製情境、生成後續提問與評估對話。為方便各種終端直接複製，範例觀察描述使用英文。 uv run lladar create situation --instructions \"Observe whether the assistant remains consistent about needing an order number across a follow-up conversation and avoids inventing order status\" --stop-criteria \"Continue until at least two user messages have been sent and the assistant has replied to the follow-up, or stop at the maximum turn limit\" --max-turns 3 --output .tmp/situation-site-demo/situation.json --model gemini:gemini-3.8-flash uv run lladar run-agent --situation-config .tmp/situation-site-demo/situation.json --project example_project/situation_demo --num-scenarios 2 --output .tmp/situation-site-demo/transcripts.jsonl --model gemini:gemini-3.8-flash uv run lladar eval .tmp/situation-site-demo/transcripts.jsonl --situation-config .tmp/situation-site-demo/situation.json --output .tmp/situation-site-demo/evaluation.json --model gemini:gemini-3.8-flash uv run lladar report .tmp/situation-site-demo/evaluation.json --output .tmp/situation-site-demo/report.md 再次執行時請改用新路徑；確定要覆寫既有檔案時才加 --force 。若行為需要文件依據，可在建立情境時重複加上 --knowledge PATH ；目前接受已存在的 .md 或 .txt 檔案。"},{"heading":"情境設定檔固定哪些內容？","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"situation.json 保存觀察行為、停止描述與最多輪次、知識檔雜湊、固定限制、宣告的變化軸和值、三階段有版本的方法指示，以及評分規準。 create situation --instructions 仍一次規劃完整流程，也可用 --skill DIRECTORY 客製編製方法。情境 run-agent 保留固定執行方法並拒絕排程 Skill；eval 預設使用固定 rubric，也可用互斥的 --criteria TEXT 或 --skill DIRECTORY 重評保存的對話。原始 config 不變，結果記錄實際評估設定。 每個具體情境都記錄選用的變化與第一則使用者訊息；後續提問依受測目標的真實回覆產生。受測目標只會收到使用者訊息，不會收到隱藏的觀察條件或 rubric。"},{"heading":"正式測試前先校準多輪 adapter","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"專案可自行提供 lladar_session.py ；沒有時，LLaDAR 會在專案副本中產生候選 adapter。兩種專案模式共用 coding Agent 的讀檔、搜尋、Graphify、公開入口選擇與實跑修復。 max_turns=1 只校準單輪真實回答，不要求記憶；多輪設定才先在同一個 session 送兩輪：第二輪必須記得第一輪的隨機代碼；再開新 session，確認識別碼不同且不能取回舊代碼。每個請求和回覆也要正確對應 session ID 與 turn ID。校準失敗就不執行正式情境，原因存於 transcripts.jsonl.calibration.json 。 adapter 從 stdin 逐行讀入 JSON，並在 stdout 逐行回傳 JSON。 open 建立 session 並宣告隔離及是否可延續（多輪才要求可延續）； send 回傳真正的最終回答與相同識別碼； close 結束 session。每個試次使用獨立的專案副本和程序。診斷訊息寫到 stderr，stdout 只輸出 JSONL。範例專案內有可執行的應用與 adapter。 {\"op\":\"open\",\"trial_id\":\"scenario-001-trial-1\"} {\"op\":\"send\",\"session_id\":\"abc123\",\"turn_id\":\"scenario-001-trial-1-turn-1\",\"message\":\"Where is my order?\"} {\"op\":\"close\",\"session_id\":\"abc123\"} 對應的 stdout 範例（ abc123 僅示意；實際 session ID 每次開啟都應不同）： {\"session_id\":\"abc123\",\"persistent\":true,\"isolated\":true} {\"session_id\":\"abc123\",\"turn_id\":\"scenario-001-trial-1-turn-1\",\"output\":\"Please provide an order number.\"} {\"closed\":\"abc123\"} 明確指定 --service-url URL 時，adapter 會透過 LLADAR_SERVICE_URL 收到該位址，必須呼叫服務的公開 API 並保留對話識別。仍需專案原始碼或自行提供的 adapter 才能理解 API 契約；單獨一個 URL 不夠。目前 --page-url 尚不支援多輪情境。"},{"heading":"檢查過程與結果","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"檔案 用途 situation.json 固定方法、rubric、變化軸、停止規則和知識來源雜湊。 transcripts.jsonl 每行一個完整試次，包含各輪對答和停止原因。 transcripts.jsonl.scenarios.jsonl 生成的情境起點與所選變化。 transcripts.jsonl.turns.jsonl 每輪使用者訊息與受測目標回答。 transcripts.jsonl.calibration.json adapter 的多輪延續與隔離校準。 transcripts.jsonl.run.json 設定及 adapter 雜湊、數量、錯誤和介接來源。 evaluation.json 情境有效性、行為判斷與引用的 turn ID。 report.md 統計與各試次證據表。 觀察到行為的比例只計入完成、有效且可判定的試次；錯誤和證據不足不會被算成「未觀察到」。2026-10-02 的本地 Gemini 實跑中，兩個情境各完成兩輪，並都被判為有效且觀察到行為；這只是該次保存結果，不保證未來生成結果相同。"},{"heading":"客製情境編製方法","anchor":"doc-search-section-6","text":"將內建的 SKILL.md 複製到自己的目錄，修改編製指示，再用 create situation --skill DIRECTORY 指定。請保留 submit_situation 契約，讓主程式驗證並保存設定。以下是目前隨套件提供的完整檔案；保留原始英文內容，方便直接複製： 內建 create-situation/SKILL.md --- name: create-situation description: Compile an observation into a reusable multi-turn situation configuration. --- # Situation authoring Read instructions (observe is its legacy alias), stop_criteria, max_turns, and optional knowledge. Compile the overall instructions into generation, execution, stopping and default evaluation methods. Knowledge is evidence data; the user's task instructions do not change your submission tool contract. Call submit_situation exactly once with one object named value. It must contain: - observable_conditions: a nonempty list of concrete target-response signals. - fixed_constraints: a list of facts or task features to preserve across variants. - variation_axes: a list of declared axes. Each axis has a short id and at least two distinct string values. Choose generic axes relevant to the observation; do not hard-code a population or domain. - generation_method, run_method, evaluation_method: each has id, version, and instructions as nonempty strings. Generation instructions create distinct scenario setups and first user messages. Run instructions decide the next ordinary user message after observing the target. Evaluation instructions assess the saved transcript against the fixed rubric and cite turn IDs. - rubric: a nonempty list of criteria, each with id, observed_when, invalid_when. Base criteria on target-visible evidence. Do not invent a correct answer. The host owns schema validation, max-turn enforcement, knowledge hashes, target requests, and all output files. Do not call the target or judge outcomes now."}]},{"url":"zh-TW/index.html","lang":"zh-TW","title":"把「Agent 有沒有做好事」變成能重複執行的測試","sections":[{"heading":"","anchor":"","text":"LLaDAR 文件 LLaDAR 可以依文件出題核對答案，也能在沒有知識文件時生成多輪情境，觀察既有 Agent 或應用服務的行為並產生報告。 從開始使用看起 查看完整範例"},{"heading":"你可以用它做什麼？","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":""},{"heading":"從文件產生測試題","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"提供要依據的知識文件，LLaDAR 會產生可用來測試 Agent 的題目和預期答案。 了解如何出題"},{"heading":"自動把題目交給 Agent","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"讓 LLaDAR 讀取專案，找出如何呼叫 Agent，確認可行後逐題執行。 了解如何執行"},{"heading":"逐題檢查回答","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"把每題的預期答案和 Agent 實際回答放在一起檢查，再自動統計結果。 了解如何評估"},{"heading":"產生可閱讀的報告","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"把結果、每題明細、使用的資料和限制整理成報告，方便回頭查。 了解如何產生報告"},{"heading":"一個完整情境：測試既有的客服 Agent","anchor":"doc-search-section-6","text":"假設你已經有一個客服 Agent，想知道它面對退貨、出貨和退款問題時，會不會依照公司的規則回答。你可以把客服政策交給 LLaDAR：它先依政策出題，再把題目送給 Agent，最後告訴你哪些題目答對、哪些需要改善。 1 準備知識和題目 用客服政策產生測試資料 2 執行 Agent 讓 Agent 回答每一題 3 檢查回答 比較預期答案和實際回答 4 閱讀報告 看整體結果和每題明細"},{"heading":"另一條路：用多輪情境觀察行為","anchor":"doc-search-section-7","text":"只要描述觀察行為、停止條件與最多輪次，就能建立情境設定。LLaDAR 先校準 session adapter，再依受測回覆生成後續提問並保存整段對話。 閱讀多輪情境指南 →"},{"heading":"想改變流程，也可以","anchor":"doc-search-section-8","text":"單題流程可在各階段指定自己的 SKILL.md ；多輪情境則在 create situation 時把方法編入同一份設定檔。例如，你可以規定出題時只問某些主題、評估時必須檢查哪些規則，或要求報告使用團隊慣用的格式。調整後，LLaDAR 仍會保留過程中的檔案，並由 Python 計算統計結果。 建立並使用自訂 Skill 範本"},{"heading":"開始前要準備什麼？","anchor":"doc-search-section-9","text":"單題測試需要可作為依據的文件；多輪情境的知識文件選填。兩者都需要可運作的受測目標與已設定好的 LLaDAR provider。範例 Agent 不需要另外安裝套件；但產生題目和評估回答仍會使用你設定的 provider。 查看開始使用的完整步驟"}]},{"url":"zh-TW/reference/cli.html","lang":"zh-TW","title":"命令與參數參考","sections":[{"heading":"作業結果報告","anchor":"doc-search-section-1","text":"每次 CLI 主流程或 Skill 範本命令成功、失敗、取消或需要人工確認後，都自動嘗試產生 UTF-8 Markdown 報告。包含情境模式；help、版本查詢及 Python API 不產生此報告。 報告沿用 --lang ，列出狀態、退出碼、時間、允許記錄的設定、輸入路徑、已知統計、產物、經清理的問題與下一步，區分新增、修改與既有檔案。本次失敗提供工作階段資訊時才附續跑指引。答案不正確是評估結果；執行或判斷錯誤才列為作業問題。 artifacts/evaluation.json 對應 artifacts/evaluation.json.operation.md ；範本目錄 lladar-skills/eval 對應目錄旁的 lladar-skills/eval.operation.md 。已有報告時使用 .operation-2.md 、 .operation-3.md ，即使 --force 也保留歷次報告。輸出位置未解析或無法寫入時，退回原工作目錄的 .lladar/operation-reports/STAGE.operation.md 。 不增加模型呼叫，也不改退出碼。 --no-verbose 仍顯示報告位置；日誌啟用後也記入 --log 。報告省略原始提示詞、回答、URL、憑證與任意例外訊息，搭配日誌及生成／評估證據使用。兩處都無法寫入時顯示警告；程序被強制終止時無法保證產生報告。"},{"heading":"出題 token 用量（v0.17.0）","anchor":"doc-search-section-2","text":"create test-dataset 累計原生 Akasha 模型呼叫中供應商回報的輸入／輸出用量，涵蓋知識盤點、知識點對齊、出題、複查、覆蓋率審查、補題與重試。透過 LangChain callback 讀取既有回應，不會另外發出生成或 token 計數請求。重複傳送的提示詞、對話歷史與工具結果，依供應商回報再次計入輸入量。 預設開啟 --verbose ，每次模型回應後以 [TOKENS] 顯示累計輸入、輸出、合計與未回報用量的呼叫數。 --no-verbose 隱藏更新，但仍保存用量；啟用 --log 時也保存已顯示的更新。等待回應時不會逐 token 更新。 --max-input-tokens 等參數是額度上限，不是已消耗用量。 保存欄位 意思 input_tokens / output_tokens 供應商回報的累計輸入與輸出 token。 total_tokens 輸入與輸出 token 相加。 cached_input_tokens / reasoning_output_tokens 供應商提供的快取輸入／推理輸出子項，不可再加進總量；零也可能表示供應商沒有提供細項。 reported_calls / unreported_calls / failed_calls 有有效用量、沒有可用用量，以及失敗的呼叫數。失敗呼叫可能同時屬於前兩類之一。 stages 依工作流程階段分組的相同統計。 status reported ：已觀察的呼叫都有可用用量； partial ：部分呼叫或歷史作業的用量未知； unavailable ：沒有取得可用用量。 historical_usage_unknown 續跑工作階段中，較早的作業尚未啟用 token 統計。 token_usage 物件保存在 \u003coutput>.generation.json 與工作階段檢查點。作業報告列出總量、分階段統計、限制及本次執行新增的用量。續跑接續工作階段總量，不重算已保存的成果；從 sidecar 產生覆蓋率報告時，也會附上保存的用量。 未回報用量表示未知，不代表零。失敗請求、供應商內部重試及啟用統計前的作業可能無法取得用量；未發出相容 callback 的自訂整合也可能沒有用量。這些數字涵蓋出題流程，不是帳單，也不是另外執行受測 Agent、評估或產生報告的用量總和。"},{"heading":"語言設定： --lang CODE","anchor":"doc-search-section-3","text":"所有流程、Skill 範本命令與 help 都接受此選項。新工作預設 en ，包含生成敘述。 en 、 zh-TW 、 ja （別名 jp ／ Jp ）、 ko 、 zh-CN 提供完整介面、固定報告標題與離線範本資源。 其他有效代碼如 fr 交由模型理解，介面、固定標題與範本使用英文並顯示簡短提示。接受代碼不代表模型一定支援。代碼由英文字母與可選的連字號分隔英數子標籤組成。 lladar --lang ja --help lladar create test-dataset --knowledge knowledge.md --lang zh-TW --output dataset.jsonl lladar run-agent dataset.jsonl --project ../my-agent --lang zh-TW lladar eval responses.jsonl --lang zh-TW lladar report evaluation.json --lang ko 保存的問題、受測回答、引文、ID、欄位名稱、精確 probe 與數值保留原值。網站答案擷取保留原回答；技術診斷與第三方追蹤可能保留原始語言。情境模式自由文字使用指定語言；此選項不增加受測 Agent 語言要求或評分條件。 下一步命令帶上語言。新階段省略時使用 en ； --resume 省略語言時恢復保存值，明確指定時須相同。衝突會被拒絕；舊工作沒有語言紀錄時請使用原版本或建立新工作。Python 階段 API 接受 lang=\"ja\" 。紀錄區分 lang 與 ui_lang ；範本的 language.json 另記錄 template_lang 。"},{"heading":"輸出路徑","anchor":"doc-search-section-4","text":"所有主要階段都可省略 --output ，也可指定資料夾或完整檔案路徑。 省略時輸出到目前工作目錄下的 runs/ ：資料集使用 test-dataset-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.jsonl ， 其他階段依序使用 situation.json 、 responses.jsonl 、 evaluation.json 、 report.md 。 指定 --output ./artifacts 時，預設檔名與附屬檔都放進 ./artifacts/ 。 既有資料夾、結尾分隔符號或沒有副檔名的新路徑視為資料夾； 既有檔案或有副檔名的新路徑視為檔案。含點號的新資料夾可寫成 ./results.v1/ 。 既有輸出仍需 --force 。 每個階段成功後都會顯示工作摘要，列出輸出的絕對目錄、各檔案位置與內容簡述， 以及下一步命令或閱讀提示。 --no-verbose 仍會顯示摘要， --log 也會同步保存。"},{"heading":"共用選項","anchor":"doc-search-section-5","text":"lladar --version 顯示已安裝的套件版本。在工作流程命令後或命令前加上 --log PATH ，將終端輸出同步保存為新的 UTF-8 檔案。log 包含已輸出的進度、trace、摘要與已處理的錯誤，移除顏色控制碼； --no-verbose 會同時減少終端與 log 的詳細訊息。自動建立上層目錄；既有 log 會保留， --force 也不會覆寫。 lladar create test-dataset --knowledge policy/ --output dataset.jsonl --log logs/create.log 技術參考 這裡列出目前 LLaDAR 的每個命令、參數、預設值和使用時機。想了解整體流程請看使用指南；需要查精確參數時看這一頁。"},{"heading":"命令一覽","anchor":"doc-search-section-6","text":"命令 用途 主要輸出 lladar create test-dataset 從知識文件建立題目與預期答案。 資料集 JSONL 與 .generation.json 。 lladar create situation 把觀察行為與停止條件編成可重用的情境設定；知識文件選填。 情境 JSON。 lladar run-agent 執行單題資料集或多輪情境。 單題回答或多輪對話 JSONL，以及各自的執行 sidecar。 lladar eval 檢查已完成的回答。 評估 JSON。 lladar report 把評估結果輸出為 Markdown。 Markdown 報告。"},{"heading":"plan","anchor":"doc-search-section-7","text":"用自然語言描述想測的事情，讓 planner 釐清必要資訊，並將需求整理成可驗證的 PlanSpec 。它是規劃器，不是執行器：不會呼叫受測目標、自動登入、保存憑證，也不會執行後續階段。 lladar plan [REQUIREMENT] [OPTIONS] 可以省略需求文字，直接啟動互動式規劃；若提供文字，會作為對話起點。 lladar plan \"我想測客服是否依退款文件回答\" --lang zh-TW lladar plan --output runs/refund-plan --debug --log runs/refund-plan/plan.log 參數 預設值 用途 REQUIREMENT 無 測試目標的自然語言描述；可在互動對話中補充。 --output DIRECTORY runs/plan-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS 計畫包目錄；既有目錄不會覆寫。 --model MODEL 模型 profile 只指定規劃模型，不會自動指定後續階段的模型。 --env-file PATH .env 規劃模型 provider 的環境檔。 --lang CODE en 規劃對話、摘要與產物的語言。 --debug 關閉 顯示即時去敏化診斷事件。 --log PATH 計畫目錄內的 plan.log 另存結構化事件 log；既有 log 會保留。 計畫包通常包含 plan.md 、 plan.json 、 plan-events.jsonl 與 plan.log 。 ready 會另外提供 commands.ps1 ； blocked 或 failed 會提供 diagnostics.json 。 ready 代表本機輸入、能力組合、命令參數與階段依賴通過靜態檢查，不代表受測 Agent 可連線或測試已成功。 blocked 表示缺少必要輸入或能力； failed 表示規劃或產物處理發生錯誤。執行前請先閱讀計畫摘要與診斷。"},{"heading":"資料集生成方法","anchor":"doc-search-section-8","text":"選定 Skill 指引直接問答或選用圖譜。Python 可產生或修正候選，各交付方式都須通過最終驗證。JSONL 格式不變， .graph.json 為選用產物。"},{"heading":"create test-dataset","anchor":"doc-search-section-9","text":"從一或多個知識檔案或資料夾產生測試資料。 lladar create test-dataset (--knowledge PATH | --from-github URL) [OPTIONS] 參數 預設值 用途 --knowledge PATH 未提供 --from-github 時必填；可重複 知識檔案或資料夾；重複指定可合併多份輸入。 --from-github URL 未提供 --knowledge 時必填 探索公開 GitHub repo 的實際資料集，自動保存逐題查驗報告。 --skill DIRECTORY 本機： knowledge-point-qa ；GitHub： github-dataset 一個包含 SKILL.md 的本機出題方法目錄。 --output PATH . 產物目錄，會自動命名為 test-dataset-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.jsonl ；若路徑以 .jsonl 結尾，則直接使用該檔名。 --count N 0 最多保留幾筆去重後資料； 0 表示保留全部候選題目。 --seed SEED 0 固定候選題目的隨機排序。 --model MODEL gemini:gemini-3.7-flash 產生資料集使用的模型。 --env-file PATH .env 提供給模型 provider 的環境檔。 --temperature TEMPERATURE 0.0 出題時的模型取樣溫度。 --max-input-tokens N 所選模型設定 覆寫模型設定的輸入 token 上限。 --max-output-tokens N 所選模型設定 覆寫模型設定的輸出 token 上限。 --auto-window-ratio RATIO 所選模型設定 覆寫自動 context window 的比例。 --force 關閉 允許覆寫既有輸出檔。 --verbose / --no-verbose 開啟 顯示或隱藏進度、出題 trace 與累計 token 更新；隱藏更新時仍保存用量，詳見 用量統計 。 lladar create test-dataset --knowledge policy/ --knowledge faq.md --count 30 --seed 7 --output artifacts/dataset.jsonl"},{"heading":"create situation","anchor":"doc-search-section-10","text":"把觀察行為、停止規則、宣告的變化軸及固定評分方法編成情境 JSON；知識文件選填，與三欄單題 QA 資料集分開。 lladar create situation (--instructions TEXT | --instructions-file PATH) (--stop-criteria TEXT | --stop-criteria-file PATH) --max-turns N [--output PATH] [OPTIONS] 參數 預設值 用途 --instructions TEXT / --instructions-file PATH 必須選一個 整體生成、執行與預設評估指示，直接輸入或讀取 UTF-8 檔案；兩者互斥。舊 --observe／--observe-file 保留為別名。 --stop-criteria TEXT / --stop-criteria-file PATH 必須選一個 直接輸入語意停止規則，或從 UTF-8 檔案讀入；兩者互斥。 --max-turns N 必填 每個情境正整數的最多對答輪次。 --knowledge PATH 無；可重複 已存在的 .md 或 .txt 檔案；記錄路徑與雜湊，執行及評估時再次核對。 --output PATH situation.json 情境 JSON 路徑；已有檔案時須加 --force 才能覆寫。 --skill DIRECTORY 內建 create-situation 編製這份情境設定的本機 SKILL.md 。 --model MODEL gemini:gemini-3.7-flash 編製情境使用的模型。 --env-file PATH .env provider 的環境檔。 --force 關閉 覆寫已有的設定檔。 lladar create situation --instructions \"資訊不足時請求訂單編號，避免編造狀態\" --stop-criteria \"完成追問回答或達最多輪次就停止\" --max-turns 3 --output artifacts/situation.json 產物保存觀察和停止文字、知識雜湊、生成及執行方法、變化軸與評分規準。完整範例請看 多輪情境指南 。"},{"heading":"run-agent","anchor":"doc-search-section-11","text":"透過已檢查的專案或已校正的問答網頁執行 Agent，先驗證入口，再把回答填入新結果檔的 actual_response 。"},{"heading":"目標參數怎麼選？","anchor":"doc-search-section-12","text":"單用 --project PATH 也可能足夠：LLaDAR 從原始碼與文件理解對外介面及啟動方式。必要執行環境設定完整時，可以在隔離的專案副本中啟動需要的服務，最後只關閉自己啟動的服務。啟動、驗證或 API 契約資訊不足時會要求補充。 要使用已啟動的測試服務時，才加上 --service-url URL 。它提供的是基底位址，不是啟動指令，也不是 HTTP 方法、路徑、Payload 或回應格式；這些仍靠專案探索理解。LLaDAR 不會啟動或關閉該既有服務。參數名稱是 --service-url ，不是 --service-api 。 若只有正常問答網頁、沒有專案原始碼，改用 --page-url URL ：瀏覽器登入、校正與錄製請求供重播，再由模型抽取回應文字。不能與 --project 或 --service-url 合用；未指定專案或網頁時預設檢查目前目錄。詳見 三種方式的選擇指南 。 lladar run-agent DATASET [OPTIONS] lladar run-agent --situation-config PATH --num-scenarios N [OPTIONS] 參數 預設值 用途 DATASET 單題模式必填 輸入 JSONL；其中的 actual_response 必須是 null；使用 --situation-config 時省略。 --project PATH . 要檢查並複製到隔離工作區的 Agent 專案；與 --page-url 二選一。 --page-url URL 無 正常問答頁面；固定引導登入、校正、授權與 MATCH，開瀏覽器前要求 stdin、stderr 為終端，不需互動旗標。 --output PATH responses.jsonl 主要 JSONL。單題模式另有 PATH.trials.jsonl 與 PATH.run.json ；情境模式另有 PATH.scenarios.jsonl 、 PATH.turns.jsonl 、 PATH.calibration.json 與 PATH.run.json 。 --skill DIRECTORY 內建 run-agent-stability 一個包含 SKILL.md 的本機排程方法目錄。 --situation-config PATH 無 使用固定的情境 JSON，省略 DATASET；不能與 --skill 合用。 --num-scenarios N 無 情境模式必填的正整數具體情境數。 --seed SEED 0 單題模式固定選題順序。 --model MODEL gemini:gemini-3.8-flash 專案 coding model；瀏覽器抽取預設 gemini:gemini-3.8-flash（目前支援 Gemini API）。 --env-file PATH .env 提供給 coding model provider 與目標程式的環境檔；既有環境變數優先。 --target-python PATH 單題：尋找 PROJECT/.venv ；情境：專案 venv 或目前 Python 目標專案使用的 Python 執行檔。 --timeout SECONDS 3600 （60 分鐘） 每個 adapter、工具子程序或瀏覽器 request 的最長秒數；不會提高模型抽取的獨立限制。 --max-tool-calls N 100 每次探索或 adapter 修復最多可呼叫幾個工具。 --graphify / --no-graphify 開啟 開啟或關閉來源探索前的選用靜態程式碼圖。 --graphify-python PATH 自動尋找既有 uv tool 環境 含有 graphifyy 的 Python 執行檔。 --service-url URL 無 已啟動測試服務的 base URL；只適用 --project ，不會理解任意 API URL。 --confirm-browser-run 關閉 只預先核准瀏覽器驗證題和已排程 request；不核准模型傳輸，也不能略過終端校正與 MATCH。 --allow-response-model-transfer 關閉 核准本次將真實回應內容傳至 --model；N 次試跑最多 N+2 次模型呼叫，每次 8,192 輸出 tokens、共用 60 分鐘。不核准網站請求，也不跳過獨立核對。 --max-input-tokens N / --max-output-tokens N 所選模型的額度設定 僅覆寫專案 auto-adapter 的探索、生成與修復額度，必須大於零；不改變受測 Agent 或瀏覽器擷取設定。預設 Gemini 3.8 Flash 為 1,048,576 input／65,536 output tokens。 --fresh-browser-profile 關閉 本次使用暫時的全新登入 profile，不重用該站既有 session。 --interactive / --no-interactive 專案模式：只有 TTY 時開啟 允許或禁止專案入口選擇提示；與 --page-url 合用會被拒絕，網站模式固定採終端引導流程。 --force 關閉 覆寫既有回答檔和附帶紀錄檔。 --verbose / --no-verbose 開啟 顯示或隱藏進度與 coding Agent trace。 lladar run-agent artifacts/dataset.jsonl --project path/to/agent --no-interactive --output artifacts/responses.jsonl lladar run-agent artifacts/dataset.jsonl --project path/to/agent --service-url http://127.0.0.1:8000 --output artifacts/responses.jsonl lladar run-agent artifacts/dataset.jsonl --page-url https://example.test/chat --output artifacts/responses.jsonl 瀏覽器啟動、首次導頁及重新導頁各自最多等 300 秒（5 分鐘），不受 --timeout 影響。網站回答仍預設等 60 分鐘，自動重播另受整輪剩餘期限約束。 僅保留模型直接抽取；預設 gemini:gemini-3.8-flash。一次 YES 同意所揭露的網站請求與真實回應外傳後，才讀取 GEMINI_API_KEY／GOOGLE_API_KEY。兩個核准旗標保留各自範圍，兩者都提供才免授權提示，仍不能跳過 MATCH。驗證題改在彩色 terminal（stderr）核對全文，不開 HTML 分頁；NO_COLOR 或 TERM=dumb 改用純文字。拒絕重新導向核對輸出，終端捲動紀錄可能留存內容；登入與擷取仍需瀏覽器。模型輸入上限為含封裝的 120 KiB UTF-8 JSON；超限不截斷、不重試。抽取合法不等於忠實或答案正確。詳見 執行指南 。"},{"heading":"情境執行契約","anchor":"doc-search-section-13","text":"專案可提供 lladar_session.py ，或由 LLaDAR 在專案副本中產生候選程式。正式測試前必須通過同一 session 兩輪及新 session 隔離校準。指定的 --service-url 會透過 LLADAR_SERVICE_URL 傳入，adapter 必須呼叫真正的公開 API。情境模式不支援 --page-url 。run JSON 記錄 adapter 雜湊、來源和錯誤。詳見 校準流程 。 lladar run-agent --situation-config artifacts/situation.json --project example_project/situation_demo --num-scenarios 2 --output artifacts/transcripts.jsonl"},{"heading":"eval","anchor":"doc-search-section-14","text":"用評估方法檢查已完成的回答，並由保存下來的逐題判斷計算彙總結果。 lladar eval RESPONSES [OPTIONS] 參數 預設值 用途 RESPONSES 必填 run-agent 產生的單題回答或情境對話 JSONL。 --output PATH evaluation.json 要產生的評估 JSON。 --criteria TEXT 無 給內建方法的評估需求；與 --skill 互斥。 --skill DIRECTORY 無 包含標準與步驟的完整本機評估方法；也取代 typed／probe 預設評分。 --situation-config PATH 無 核對原始執行與設定雜湊，預設使用固定 rubric；--criteria 或 --skill 可替換評估，保留原始 config。 --model MODEL gemini:gemini-2.5-flash 評估 Agent 使用的模型。 --env-file PATH .env 提供給評估 provider 的環境檔。 --strict 關閉 任一筆評估出錯就停止；不加時會把該筆記成 judge error，繼續其他資料。 --force 關閉 覆寫既有評估檔。 --max-input-tokens N / --max-output-tokens N 所選模型 profile 兩種模式的評估計畫與判斷所用的正整數 token 上限；保存於評估 JSON。 --verbose / --no-verbose 開啟 設定、逐題進度、模型等待提示、判斷狀態與耗時；--log 保存相同訊息。 lladar eval artifacts/responses.jsonl --strict --output artifacts/evaluation.json 兩者都不指定時沿用既有預設。結果與報告保存實際模式、準則全文與雜湊，或 Skill 來源與資源證據；只有正確性維度才產生正確率表。 lladar eval artifacts/responses.jsonl --criteria \"觀察目標用詞；命中不等同偏見\" --output artifacts/wording-evaluation.json"},{"heading":"情境評估結果","anchor":"doc-search-section-15","text":"情境評估保存有效性、行為判斷、引用的 turn ID 和確定性統計；失敗或無法判定的試次不計入觀察比例。 lladar eval artifacts/transcripts.jsonl --situation-config artifacts/situation.json --output artifacts/situation-evaluation.json"},{"heading":"report","anchor":"doc-search-section-16","text":"把評估輸出轉為不誇大結論、可回頭查的 Markdown 報告。 lladar report EVALUATION [OPTIONS] 參數 預設值 用途 EVALUATION 必填 eval 產生的評估 JSON。 --output PATH report.md 要產生的 Markdown 報告。 --skill DIRECTORY 單題：內建 report-evidence-summary ；情境：無 本機報告方法；情境模式只增加敘述，不改已保存的判斷與統計。 --model MODEL gemini:gemini-3.7-flash 用 skill 撰寫摘要的模型；情境報告未指定 --skill 時不呼叫模型。 --env-file PATH .env 提供給報告 provider 的環境檔。 --force 關閉 覆寫既有報告。 lladar report artifacts/evaluation.json --output artifacts/report.md"},{"heading":"Skill 範本（進階）","anchor":"skill-templates","text":"想自訂出題、情境編製、測試排程、評估或報告撰寫方式時，可用 lladar create --help 中的五個命令建立可編輯的 Skill。建立範本會在本機寫入檔案，無須呼叫模型。編輯後，在對應的工作流程用 --skill DIRECTORY 指向範本目錄。 建立範本的命令 可自訂的內容 在哪個命令使用 --skill lladar create test-dataset-skill 出題範圍、問句風格、預期答案要求。 lladar create test-dataset lladar create situation-skill 多輪情境的觀察目標、可變條件，以及哪些對話證據算成功或失敗。 lladar create situation lladar create run-agent-skill 單題測試的選題方式與重複次數，例如抽五題、每題測三次。 lladar run-agent 的單題模式 lladar create eval-skill 回答的判定規則，例如同義說法是否可接受、哪些條件必須答到。 lladar eval 。使用 --skill 時省略 --criteria 。 lladar create report-skill 報告的讀者、語氣與敘述重點。統計來自已保存的評估結果。 lladar report SKILL.md 保存執行時會讀取的規則。可先看 AUTHORING.md 的修改位置與範例，再在 SKILL.md 用自然語言調整需求，並保留工具與提交格式。 language.json 記錄範本的語言設定。 --output DIRECTORY 指定範本目錄。省略時建立在目前工作目錄的 ./lladar-skills/\u003cstage>/ ，例如 ./lladar-skills/test-dataset/ 。 --lang CODE 選擇範本語言，預設 en 。使用 --lang zh-TW 建立繁體中文版。 --force 允許在既有目錄重新產生範本，會覆寫 SKILL.md 、 AUTHORING.md 和 language.json ，包括手動修改。預設遇到既有目錄會停止。 例如，先建立繁體中文的出題範本。 lladar create test-dataset-skill --output ./my-qa --lang zh-TW 在 ./my-qa/SKILL.md 修改出題規則，例如「用顧客的口吻詢問退款期限，預期答案要保留適用條件」。準備好知識文件 knowledge.md 後，使用這份 Skill 出題。 lladar create test-dataset --knowledge knowledge.md --skill ./my-qa --output dataset.jsonl --lang zh-TW"}]}]};
